/pcm_s24le/pcm_s32le (RIFX ..be), 3 pcm_f32le, 6 pcm_alaw, 7 pcm_mulaw, 0x55 mp3 (D17 pcm_s16le)\n  49 44 33 / ff fb|f3|e3 = mp3; ff f1|f9 ADTS aac; 4f 67 67 53 OggS -> OpusHead/\\x01vorbis/\\x7fFLAC; 66 4c 61 43 flac;\n  .. 66 74 79 70 (ftyp) -> stsd mp4a=aac / alac / Opus; mvhd time = s since 1904; 1a 45 df a3 MKV CodecID A_OPUS->opus\n  VIDEO: trak hdlr `vide` -> stsd avc1/hvc1/vp09/av01 w,h u16BE @entry+32 = `<w>x<h>` (D18 320x180); cross-check tkhd\n     16.16 w/h + matrix (rotation), pasp SAR, clap, SPS crop -- may disagree (\"crops\"); stills (jpg/png) = 1 video stream\n  #!AMR amr_nb|amr_wb; FORM..AIFF pcm_s16be (AIFC sowt=le); 30 26 b2 75 ASF wmav2. Truth: tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/.../ffmpeg -i f\n1f 8b 08 GZIP: FNAME if flg&8, MTIME u32LE@4, OS@9, ISIZE last 4 | \"ustar\"@257 TAR: tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(b))\n37 7a bc af 27 1c / 52 61 72 21 1a 07 00|01 00   7z (ver @6/@7; 7z l -slt) / RAR4|RAR5\n\"CD001\" @0x8001                   ISO     PVD @0x8000: system id @+8, volume id @+40, creation date @+813\n\"conectix\" last 512 / vhdxfile / KDMV / QFI\\xfb  VHD/VHDX/VMDK/QCOW2   qemu-img info --output=json\n53 51 4c 69 74 65 20 66 6f 72 6d 61 74 20 33 00  SQLite page size u16BE@16; sqlite3 .deserialize(b)\nd4 c3 b2 a1 / a1 b2 c3 d4 / 0a 0d 0d 0a  PCAP/PCAPNG  linktype u32 @20; capinfos -M; dpkt\n-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE----- / 30 82 ..  X.509   cryptography x509 load_*; openssl x509 -noout -text -fingerprint -sha256\nReceived: / Message-ID: / MIME-Version:  EML (GM fmt `email`)  lib.meta.prebuilt.eml.eml_value(b, {\"field\": f}); values VERBATIM\n  (Message-ID keeps <>); first hop = LAST Received; threads: References[0] / In-Reply-To; parts: msg.walk()\n\"From \"@0 MBOX: split on ^From , unescape >From | BEGIN:VCALENDAR/VCARD ICS/VCF: unfold CRLF+space, KEY;PARAM:value\nef bb bf / ff fe / fe ff          BOM     text.*_bom_present\nTime fields: FILETIME = 100ns since 1601 (/1e7 - 11644473600); WebKit = us since 1601; PRTime = us since 1970;\n  Mac/MP4 = s since 1904; DOS date/time = 2-s resolution, local. Spelling unverified -> prefer ISO-8601 `Z` for `_utc`.\nHex fields: `0x` + lowercase, zero-padded to the STRUCT width (`_u16_hex` 4 digits, `_u32_hex` 8). GUIDs follow source.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nRanking (D18 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D19-D21 question with no extractor (or a wrong-answer bug in an existing one), or a harness blocker that silently fails a\nwhole family of prebuilds. TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"media-image-as-video-stream\", \"concept\": \"Still images asked through `media.*` (ffprobe opens JPEG/PNG/GIF/BMP/WebP as one video stream)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUG-LEVEL GAP: on the D18 TT kit, lib.meta.answer('d18-video-001-media-primary-video-dimensions', data=camera-001.jpg / panel-001.png) returns ('none','verified') and audio-001.wav returns (None, None). ffprobe reports a still as stream 0 codec_type video: JPEG -> codec_name mjpeg (demuxer jpeg_pipe/image2, pix_fmt yuvj420p/yuvj422p/yuvj444p/gray from SOF sampling), PNG -> png (rgb24/rgba/gray/ya8/pal8/rgb48be/rgba64be from IHDR bit depth+colour type), GIF -> gif (bgra), BMP -> bmp (bgr24/bgra/pal8), WebP -> webp, TIFF -> tiff. Fix in lib/meta/prebuilt (new module media_stills.py registering fmt media/video/av, or extend media_video): primary_video_dimensions(_pixels)/width/height from SOF/IHDR/LSD/DIB/VP8 headers (`<w>x<h>`, same as D4/D5), primary_video_codec_name, primary_video_pix_fmt, nb_streams 1, primary_audio_* -> `none`; an audio-only WAV/MP3 -> literal `none` for every primary_video_* field (absent stream), not None. Fixtures: the kit's jpg/png from any day18 solver case + the bundled ffmpeg -i to confirm the expected spellings offline.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"video-geometry-crop-aspect\", \"concept\": \"Crop / aspect / display geometry of the primary video stream\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 flavor 'originals, crops'. fmt media (+video/av). ffprobe semantics: width/height = decoder output = SPS size after frame_cropping (h264: (pic_width_in_mbs*16 - CropUnitX*(left+right)); hevc conf_win_*), coded_width/coded_height = MB/CTB-aligned size; sample_aspect_ratio `N:M` from pasp (else SPS VUI aspect_ratio_idc table, else `1:1`/`0:1` when unknown), display_aspect_ratio = reduced (w*sarN):(h*sarD) e.g. `16:9`. Fields: primary_video_sample_aspect_ratio, primary_video_display_aspect_ratio, primary_video_coded_width/height/dimensions, sps_dimensions_pixels, stsd_dimensions_pixels, tkhd_dimensions_pixels (16.16 -> int when whole, else 3 decimals), display_dimensions_pixels (tkhd size; swapped when |rotation| = 90), clean_aperture_dimensions (clap widthN/D, heightN/D, horizOff, vertOff), tapt_clef/prof/enof dimensions (QuickTime), mkv_pixel_crop (Top/Bottom/Left/Right) + DisplayWidth/DisplayHeight/DisplayUnit, is_cropped (true when SPS crop/clap/PixelCrop non-zero or tkhd < coded), geometry_mismatch (stsd vs SPS vs tkhd disagree). ALSO: make primary_video_dimensions prefer the SPS-cropped size when an SPS is present (ffprobe), stsd as fallback; document the choice. Fixtures: hand-pack avcC with a 1920x1088 SPS + crop_bottom 4 (-> 1920x1080) and a pasp 4:3 / tkhd 1440 case.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"video-device-provenance\", \"concept\": \"Claimed recording device / producer of a video (make, model, software, encoder, screen recording)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 flavor 'the recording that could not have come from the claimed device'. fmt media (+video/av/mp4/mov). Sources: QuickTime mdta keys/ilst (`com.apple.quicktime.make`, `.model`, `.software`, `.creationdate`, `.location.ISO6709`, `.camera.lens_model`), udta `\\u00a9mak`/`\\u00a9mod`/`\\u00a9swr`/`\\u00a9too`/`\\u00a9xyz`/`\\u00a9day` (2-byte len + 2-byte lang + text), Android `com.android.version`/`com.android.manufacturer`/`com.android.model`/`com.android.capture.fps`, Samsung `smta`/`SEFT`, GoPro `GPMF`/udta `FIRM`, MKV Tags/Info MuxingApp+WritingApp, AVI `ISFT`. Fields: device_make, device_model, device_software, tag_<key> for every mdta key (ffprobe prints mdta keys verbatim as tag names, e.g. `com.apple.quicktime.make`), handler_name (per stream; `Core Media Video` Apple, `VideoHandle` Android, `VideoHandler` Lavf, `ISO Media file produced by Google Inc.`), encoder (stream `encoder` from stsd compressorname Pascal string @entry+50 len<=31, e.g. `Lavc libx264`, `H.264`, `AVC Coding`; container `encoder` from \\u00a9too e.g. `Lavf61.1.100`), is_screen_recording heuristics as diagnostics only (no device keys + display-sized odd dims like 886x1920 / 1170x2532 + VFR stts). Answer verbatim strings; absent -> none. Odd-device synthesis goes to video-geometry-synthesis.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mp4-mov-atoms\", \"concept\": \"MP4/M4A/MOV/3GP atom metadata (voice memos, phone video)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (aliases audio, av, video, mp4, mov, quicktime). Box walk (size u32 BE, type; size 1 -> u64; size 0 -> to EOF). Fields: ftyp_major_brand (4 chars; emit rstrip'ed, plus ftyp_major_brand_raw verbatim), ftyp_minor_version, ftyp_compatible_brands (JSON, stored order), mvhd_creation_time_utc / mvhd_modification_time_utc (v0 u32 / v1 u64 seconds since 1904-01-01 -> ISO-8601 `Z`; ffprobe tag creation_time prints `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.000000Z`, emit that spelling under tag_creation_time), mvhd_timescale, mvhd_duration_seconds (duration/timescale, ffprobe-style 6 decimals), track_count, track_handler_types (JSON soun/vide/text), mdhd_languages (packed ISO-639-2 `und`), udta/ilst tags `\\u00a9too` encoder, `\\u00a9nam` title, `\\u00a9day`, `\\u00a9xyz` location (ISO 6709 string verbatim), mdta keys (`com.apple.quicktime.make/model/software/creationdate/location.ISO6709`) as tag_<key>. Pure struct; register via lib.meta like media_streams.py. Fixtures: build tiny m4a/mov with hand-packed boxes in the test (no ffmpeg needed). D18 video-001.mp4 (Lavf: ftyp isom/512/isomiso2avc1mp41, udta/meta hdlr mdta keys=[title] -> `Huntress MP4 evidence <12 HEX>`, handler_name VideoHandler/SoundHandler, encoder `Lavc libx264`) is a ready fixture shape; device keys feed video-device-provenance.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"video-geometry-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file video/image geometry synthesis (originals vs crops, aspect groups, impossible device)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend lib.meta.synthesis (fmt synthesis) over the question's `Files: [...]` (mp4/mov/mkv/jpg/png members; get_bytes per set like digest_order). Dimensions per file = ffprobe width x height (stills included, see media-image-as-video-stream). Fields/ids: dimension_order / pixel_area_order (ascending area, ties by name), largest_frame_file, aspect_ratio_groups (JSON object DAR -> sorted names), original_files (per correlation group the largest frame; group key = title/mdta correlation id `<12 HEX>` tag, else same duration+frame count), cropped_files (smaller than its group original or is_cropped), crop_of (JSON object crop -> original), odd_device_file (claimed make/model disagreeing with the group's majority or geometry/rotation impossible for the claimed device: portrait phone recording with identity matrix and landscape coded size, screen-sized dims with camera make), rotation_groups. Compact JSON, ascending/name order unless the text says otherwise.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"image-modern-containers\", \"concept\": \"WebP / TIFF / HEIC-AVIF / ICC under an abstract `image.*` fmt\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt image (alias also for existing jpeg/png/gif/bmp fields: image.dimensions_pixels routes by magic to SOF/IHDR/LSD/DIB) + webp, tiff, heic. WebP `RIFF....WEBP`: VP8 (frame tag, 14-bit w/h after `9d 01 2a`), VP8L (`2f` + 14-bit w-1/h-1), VP8X (canvas 24-bit w-1/h-1, flags ICC/alpha/EXIF/XMP/anim), chunk_ids JSON, has_exif/has_xmp/has_icc, animation frame_count. TIFF `II*\\\\0`/`MM\\\\0*`: byte_order, ifd0 ImageWidth/ImageLength/Make/Model/Software/DateTime/Artist, ifd_count. HEIC/AVIF `ftyp heic|heix|mif1|avif`: major_brand, ispe width x height of the primary item (pitm), item count, Exif item presence. ICC (APP2 ICC_PROFILE / PNG iCCP zlib / WebP ICCP): profile_description (desc/mluc), color_space, device_class, version. Answer formats like D4/D5: `<w>x<h>`. D18 flavor 'previews' + one-namespace-per-family drift: build together with media-image-as-video-stream (same dims parsers, fmt image AND media).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"synthesis-order-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Synthesis questions with a non-sha256 key (size/time/duration order, codec grouping)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis*.py (fmt synthesis) for ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>-order|groups|<x>` over the question's `Files: [...]` list (parse like digest_order; get_bytes per set): size_order (ascending bytes, ties -> filename), md5_order/sha1_order/sha512_order (generic algo from id), mtime_order (zip DOS mtime of each member from the container CD; also embedded timestamps: EXIF DateTimeOriginal, PDF CreationDate, email Date, mvhd creation), duration_order (media duration_seconds), codec_groups (JSON object codec_name -> sorted names), extension_mismatch_files (names whose magic != extension, file order), largest_file/smallest_file, newest_file/oldest_file. Descending only if the text says descending/newest first. Compact JSON.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-codec-params\", \"concept\": \"Codec-level parameters (AAC profile, MP3 frame/Xing/LAME, Opus/Vorbis details) in ffprobe vocabulary\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (+audio/av). Fields: primary_audio_profile (AAC AudioSpecificConfig object type from esds/ADTS: 2 -> `LC`, 5 -> `HE-AAC`, 29 -> `HE-AACv2`, 1 -> `Main`; ffprobe spelling), primary_audio_codec_long_name (ffprobe strings: `AAC (Advanced Audio Coding)`, `MP3 (MPEG audio layer 3)`, `PCM signed 16-bit little-endian`, `Opus (Opus Interactive Audio Codec)`, `Vorbis`, `FLAC (Free Lossless Audio Codec)`), mp3_mpeg_version, mp3_layer, mp3_bitrate_kbps (first frame), mp3_vbr_header (`Xing`/`Info`/`VBRI`/none), mp3_lame_encoder (9-char LAME tag e.g. `LAME3.100`), mp3_frame_count, primary_audio_sample_fmt for compressed codecs (aac/mp3 -> `fltp`, opus -> `fltp`, vorbis -> `fltp`, flac -> s16/s32 by bps). Verify spellings offline with the bundled ffmpeg -i.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D17 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set). D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings. D18: Files = note + panel-001.png + installer-001.msi + video-001.mp4; the single worker pre-wired the dispatch -> TT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"gate-allowlist-dfir-libs\", \"concept\": \"Prebuild gate refuses installed DFIR libs\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS lacks Evtx, regipy, olefile, oletools, dnfile, LnkParse3, lief, cryptography, asn1crypto, dpkt, PIL, sqlite3, wave, ordlookup. Targets evtx-records (python-evtx) and regf-values (regipy) as written will fail the gate exactly like pe-debug-rich-imports did (import ordlookup). Either widen the allowlist (all are in .venv) or rewrite those goals as stdlib/struct parsers. Also `open` is banned: regipy RegistryHive needs a path -> use a struct nk/vk walker.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"asf-aiff-caf-containers\", \"concept\": \"Other audio containers: ASF/WMA, AIFF/AIFC, CAF, AU, 3GP AMR\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (+audio/av; also fmt asf/aiff/caf aliases). Route by magic: ASF header GUID `30 26 b2 75 8e 66 cf 11 a6 d9 00 aa 00 62 ce 6c` -> Stream Properties audio WAVEFORMATEX tag (0x160 wmav1, 0x161 wmav2, 0x162 wmapro, 0x163 wmalossless, 0x0A wmavoice) + Content Description title/author/copyright/description + File Properties creation date (FILETIME) and play duration; AIFF `FORM....AIFF`/`AIFC` COMM: channels, numSampleFrames, sampleSize, 80-bit IEEE extended sample rate, AIFC compressionType (`NONE` -> pcm_s16be, `sowt` -> pcm_s16le, `fl32` -> pcm_f32be, `ulaw`/`alaw` -> pcm_mulaw/pcm_alaw, `ima4` -> adpcm_ima_qt) + NAME/AUTH/ANNO chunks; CAF `caff` desc chunk (float64 rate, formatID `lpcm`/`aac `/`alac`/`opus`/`ulaw`) + info chunk tags; Sun AU `.snd` encoding 1/2/3/27. Expose through primary_audio_codec_name/sample_rate/channels/container_format like the existing media modules (format_name ffprobe: `asf`, `aiff`, `caf`, `au`).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xmp-packets\", \"concept\": \"XMP packet fields in any container (DocumentID lineage)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt xmp (also registered under jpeg/png/pdf/media/ooxml/image as xmp_<field>). Find `<x:xmpmeta` ... `</x:xmpmeta>` (or `<?xpacket begin` ... `<?xpacket end`) anywhere in the bytes (JPEG APP1 `http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/\\\\0`, PNG iTXt `XML:com.adobe.xmp`, PDF Metadata stream if uncompressed, MP4 `uuid` BE7ACFCB-97A9-42E8-9C71-999491E3AFAC, WAV `_PMX` chunk). Parse with xml.etree (namespaces by URI, rdf:Description attributes AND child elements, rdf:Seq/Alt/Bag -> lists). Fields: document_id, instance_id, original_document_id (verbatim incl. `xmp.did:`/`uuid:` prefixes), derived_from_document_id, history_actions (JSON, stored order), history_software_agents, creator_tool, create_date, modify_date, metadata_date (verbatim), dc_creator (JSON list), dc_title (x-default), dc_format. Synthesis helper: files sharing document_id/original_document_id.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"subtitle-chapter-streams\", \"concept\": \"Cover art, subtitle and chapter streams (ffprobe stream accounting)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (+av/video). ffprobe counts an embedded cover (ID3 APIC, MP4 `covr`, FLAC PICTURE block, MKV attachment with image mime) as a VIDEO stream with codec_name `mjpeg`/`png` and disposition attached_pic=1 -> fields attached_pic_present, attached_pic_codec_name, attached_pic_mime_type, attached_pic_dimensions_pixels, nb_streams_including_cover (document the difference vs audio_stream_count). Subtitles: MP4 `tx3g` -> `mov_text`, MKV S_TEXT/UTF8 -> `subrip`, S_TEXT/ASS -> `ass`, S_TEXT/WEBVTT -> `webvtt`; fields subtitle_stream_count, subtitle_codec_names (stream order), subtitle_languages. Chapters: MP4 `chpl`/QuickTime chapter track, MKV EditionEntry/ChapterAtom -> chapter_count, chapter_titles (JSON), chapter_start_times_seconds.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"zone-identifier-motw\", \"concept\": \"Download provenance: Zone.Identifier ADS, macOS quarantine, AppleDouble\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt zone_identifier (aliases motw, ads): text `[ZoneTransfer]` INI (UTF-8/UTF-16 with BOM): zone_id (int), zone_name (0 Local,1 Intranet,2 Trusted,3 Internet,4 Restricted), referrer_url, host_url, last_writer_package_family_name, app_zone_id -- values verbatim. Member names like `x.exe:Zone.Identifier` or `x.exe_Zone.Identifier`. fmt quarantine: `com.apple.quarantine` value `flags;hex_unix_time;agent;uuid` -> quarantine_flags_hex, quarantine_time_utc, quarantine_agent, quarantine_event_uuid. fmt appledouble: `00 05 16 07` header, entry table (id 2 resource fork, 9 Finder info with `ATTR` xattr block) -> xattr_names (JSON), xattr_<name> (UTF-8 if printable else hex), finder_type_creator.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"archives-tar-7z-iso\", \"concept\": \"TAR / 7z / RAR / ISO9660-UDF headers (archives gap only produced gzip)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt archives were not registered by the earlier `archives` run (tar/7z/rar/iso have 0 fields). Separate modules: tar (ustar_magic, member_names stored order, member_sizes, member_mtimes_utc, member_modes_octal, member_unames/gnames, typeflags) via tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(b)); 7z (signature_version `0.4`, next_header_offset/size, start_header_crc32_hex, has_encrypted_header when the next header is kEncodedHeader with AES coder 06f10701); rar (version 4|5, RAR5 main archive flags, file names when headers unencrypted, is_header_encrypted); iso (pvd system_id, volume_id, volume_set_id, publisher_id, application_id (strip spaces), volume_creation_date_utc from 17-byte dec-datetime @813 with GMT offset, volume_space_size, logical_block_size, joliet_present (SVD escape %/@ %/C %/E), udf_present (BEA01/NSR02/NSR03), root_member_names). fmt `archive` alias for all.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-fmt-alias\", \"concept\": \"GM fmt `media` -> prebuilt `wav`/`mp3` fields + D17 codec name in lib\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/media.py registering fmt 'media' (aliases 'audio', 'av') that routes by MAGIC to the existing wav/mp3/gif... extractors, and registers ('media','primary_audio_codec_name') (GM-verified D17: 16-bit PCM WAV -> 'pcm_s16le') by porting challenges/day17/metadata-hear-me-out/solver/solve.py _audio_codec (RIFF/RIFX/RF64, AIFF/AIFC, fLaC, Ogg Opus/Vorbis/FLAC/Speex, AMR, .snd, MP4 stsd, Matroska CodecID, MPEG/ADTS sync). Do NOT change the pcm_s16le mapping. D16 lesson repeated: an extractor under the container's fmt word is invisible to the GM's namespace.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-stream-fields\", \"concept\": \"ffprobe-style stream/format fields for the first audio stream\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields primary_audio_sample_rate_hz (also _sample_rate), primary_audio_channels, primary_audio_channel_layout (ffprobe: mono/stereo/2.1/quad/5.1...), primary_audio_bits_per_sample (ffprobe bits_per_sample; 0 for lossy), primary_audio_sample_fmt (u8/s16/s32/flt/dbl; planar 'fltp' for aac/opus/vorbis decoders), primary_audio_bit_rate (bps integer: PCM = rate*ch*bits), primary_audio_codec_long_name ('PCM signed 16-bit little-endian'), primary_audio_codec_tag_hex ('0x0001'), primary_audio_codec_tag_string ffprobe-style, primary_audio_duration_seconds (string with 6 decimals like ffprobe '1.250000'), primary_audio_nb_samples / duration_ts, format_name (ffprobe demuxer: wav, mp3, ogg, flac, aiff, amr, au, 'mov,mp4,m4a,3gp,3g2,mj2', 'matroska,webm'), format_long_name, nb_streams, audio_stream_count, format_duration_seconds, format_size_bytes, format_bit_rate. WAV: data chunk size / byte rate; MP3: Xing/Info/VBRI frames or frame walk; Ogg: last page granule / rate (Opus 48 kHz minus pre_skip); FLAC: STREAMINFO total samples; MP4: mdhd timescale/duration.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-wav-deep\", \"concept\": \"WAV chunk-level metadata (BWF bext, fact, LIST/INFO, cue, iXML, data-vs-RIFF size, trailing bytes)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media + wav alias, fields riff_chunk_ids (file order JSON), info_title (INAM; D17 carried 'Huntress audio evidence <12 hex>'), info_software (ISFT), info_creation_date (ICRD), info_comment (ICMT), info_artist (IART), bext_description, bext_originator, bext_originator_reference, bext_origination_date, bext_origination_time, bext_time_reference, bext_umid_hex, fact_sample_count, data_chunk_size_bytes, riff_size_declared, riff_size_mismatch (declared+8 != len), trailing_bytes_after_data (count + magic_prefix_hex_16 of the trailer -> hidden payload), cue_point_count, ixml_present. Pure struct; values verbatim (strip trailing NULs).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-renamed-containers\", \"concept\": \"Renamed/transcoded audio: actual container + codec vs the extension\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields container_format (by magic: wav/rf64/aiff/mp3/ogg/flac/mp4/matroska/amr/au/adts/caf/wma-asf), declared_extension, extension_matches_content (true/false), mime_type_by_magic (audio/wav, audio/mpeg, audio/ogg, audio/flac, audio/mp4, audio/amr), plus primary_audio_codec_name for: ASF/WMA (GUID 3026b275 + stream props -> wmav2), CAF ('caff' desc fourcc), MP4 esds objectTypeIndication (0x40 aac, 0x6b mp3), Ogg multiple codecs. Flavor D17: 'Voice notes have been transcoded, renamed'.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-multistream\", \"concept\": \"Per-stream fields in multi-stream containers; the odd stream\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields stream_codec_names (JSON, container stream index order like ffprobe), audio_stream_codec_names, stream_languages (MP4 mdhd packed ISO-639-2 / MKV Language default 'eng' / 'und'), stream_titles (MKV Name, MP4 udta name/handler_name), stream_creation_times_utc (mdhd 1904 epoch), stream_durations_seconds, stream_sample_rates, primary_video_codec_name, odd_stream_index (the one whose codec/language/rate/creation_time differs from the majority -- emit index and a JSON diagnostic). MP4 box walk moov/trak/mdia/{mdhd,hdlr,minf/stbl/stsd}; Matroska EBML walk Segment/Tracks/TrackEntry (TrackType 2=audio, CodecID map A_OPUS opus, A_VORBIS vorbis, A_AAC aac, A_FLAC flac, A_MPEG/L3 mp3, A_PCM/INT/LIT pcm_s16le by BitDepth, A_AC3 ac3, V_MPEG4/ISO/AVC h264, V_MPEGH/ISO/HEVC hevc, V_VP9 vp9, V_AV1 av1); Ogg: group pages by serial, BOS packet per stream. Flavor D17: 'find the stream that breaks the sender's story'.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-format-tags\", \"concept\": \"Container/stream tags: title, artist, comment, encoder, creation_time, language\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields tag_title, tag_artist, tag_album, tag_comment, tag_encoder, tag_date, tag_creation_time_utc, tag_<key> generic (lowercase ffprobe key), encoder (ffprobe format tag 'encoder': ID3 TSSE, Vorbis/Opus ENCODER + vendor string, MP4 \\\\xa9too, MKV MuxingApp/WritingApp, WAV ISFT), opus_vendor / vorbis_vendor, id3_version. Sources: WAV LIST/INFO, ID3v2.2-2.4 (+v1), Vorbis comment (Ogg/FLAC/Opus OpusTags), MP4 moov/udta/meta/ilst, MKV Tags. Reuse prebuilt mp3/wav parsers where possible; stdlib only (mutagen is not allowlisted).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"email-media-attachments\", \"concept\": \"Audio embedded in mail: MIME audio attachments + member resolution through .eml\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email (+eml/mime aliases), fields attachment_audio_codec_names (MIME order, via the media codec extractor on decoded payloads), attachment_media_container_formats, attachment_declared_content_types, attachment_audio_mismatch_names (declared Content-Type/extension vs actual codec), attachment_audio_durations_seconds, audio_attachment_count. Also expose lib.meta.prebuilt helper attachment_bytes(eml_bytes, filename) (RFC 2231/2047 filename decode, get_payload(decode=True)) so artifact refs like `message-001.eml -> voice-001.ogg` and `zip -> eml -> wav` resolve. Flavor D17: 'embedded in mail'.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-equivalence-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-recording equivalence / odd-one-out synthesis\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Add to lib.meta.synthesis: equivalence_groups(question, get_bytes) over the `Files: [...]` audio members -> group by (1) shared title/correlation tag (WAV INAM, ID3 TIT2, Vorbis TITLE, MP4 \\\\xa9nam; D17 INAM 'Huntress audio evidence <12 hex>'), (2) equal decoded duration rounded to 10 ms / equal sample count, (3) equal PCM data-chunk sha256 or FLAC STREAMINFO MD5; outputs compact JSON array of arrays of filenames (each group sorted, groups by first name), the odd_one_out filename, duplicate_count. Also md5/sha1/size-order variants of digest_order (synthesis-siblings). Spelling unverified -> keep alternates.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tool-ffprobe\", \"concept\": \"ffprobe/ffmpeg + sox for media ground truth\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"PARTLY SOLVED: ffmpeg 7.0.2 ships at tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2 (imageio-ffmpeg; not on PATH, no ffprobe). `ffmpeg -hide_banner -i f` prints ffprobe vocabulary (`Stream #0:0: Audio: pcm_s16le ([1][0][0][0] / 0x0001), 16000 Hz, mono, s16`, format tags) -- verified on D17. Still wanted: a bin/ shim `ffmpeg` on PATH and a real ffprobe (static build) for `-show_streams -show_format -of json`; apt sox (soxi). Worker/offline verification only, never in-window. D18: the same `ffmpeg -i` line verified video geometry (`h264 (High) (avc1 / 0x31637661), yuv420p(progressive), 320x180 [SAR 1:1 DAR 16:9], 10 fps`).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"email-fmt-alias\", \"concept\": \"GM fmt `email` -> prebuilt `eml` fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/email.py re-registering EVERY ('eml', f) field of lib/meta/prebuilt/eml.py under fmt 'email' (also 'mail', 'mime') with the same extractor. D16 GM asked email.message_id; the eml-registered extractor","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/9a884a1e-870c-4737-be83-7e1c4a09a9ca/tool-results/b5bp3wmag.txt","persistedOutputSize":48135},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CBxKsjCbG3XAaWNmXuAkLR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
