{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TPsjvBGm6FRCGRtcb89EFJ","type":"tool_result","content":"## Readiness gaps\n\nRanking (D18 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D19-D21 question with no extractor (or a wrong-answer bug in an existing one), or a harness blocker that silently fails a\nwhole family of prebuilds. TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items.\n\n  {\"id\": \"media-image-as-video-stream\", \"concept\": \"Still images asked through `media.*` (ffprobe opens JPEG/PNG/GIF/BMP/WebP as one video stream)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUG-LEVEL GAP: on the D18 TT kit, lib.meta.answer('d18-video-001-media-primary-video-dimensions', data=camera-001.jpg / panel-001.png) returns ('none','verified') and audio-001.wav returns (None, None). ffprobe reports a still as stream 0 codec_type video: JPEG -> codec_name mjpeg (demuxer jpeg_pipe/image2, pix_fmt yuvj420p/yuvj422p/yuvj444p/gray from SOF sampling), PNG -> png (rgb24/rgba/gray/ya8/pal8/rgb48be/rgba64be from IHDR bit depth+colour type), GIF -> gif (bgra), BMP -> bmp (bgr24/bgra/pal8), WebP -> webp, TIFF -> tiff. Fix in lib/meta/prebuilt (new module media_stills.py registering fmt media/video/av, or extend media_video): primary_video_dimensions(_pixels)/width/height from SOF/IHDR/LSD/DIB/VP8 headers (`<w>x<h>`, same as D4/D5), primary_video_codec_name, primary_video_pix_fmt, nb_streams 1, primary_audio_* -> `none`; an audio-only WAV/MP3 -> literal `none` for every primary_video_* field (absent stream), not None. Fixtures: the kit's jpg/png from any day18 solver case + the b\n  {\"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D17 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set). D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings. D18: Files = note + panel-001.png + installer-001.msi + video-001.mp4; the single worker pre-wired the dispatch -> TT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"gate-allowlist-dfir-libs\", \"concept\": \"Prebuild gate refuses installed DFIR libs\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS lacks Evtx, regipy, olefile, oletools, dnfile, LnkParse3, lief, cryptography, asn1crypto, dpkt, PIL, sqlite3, wave, ordlookup. Targets evtx-records (python-evtx) and regf-values (regipy) as written will fail the gate exactly like pe-debug-rich-imports did (import ordlookup). Either widen the allowlist (all are in .venv) or rewrite those goals as stdlib/struct parsers. Also `open` is banned: regipy RegistryHive needs a path -> use a struct nk/vk walker.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"elf-header\", \"concept\": \"ELF header / PT_INTERP / build-id / sections\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt elf); pyelftools is allowlisted. Don't re-register e_machine_u16_hex / e_entry_hex / entry_point_hex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"macho-header\", \"concept\": \"Mach-O cputype/filetype/ncmds/LC_UUID\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt macho).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"msitools-path\", \"concept\": \"msitools present but not on PATH\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"tools/msitools/usr/bin/{msiinfo,msidump,msiextract,gcab} exist but `source bin/env.sh` doesn't expose them; add a bin/ shim. reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md still says 'Not installed: msitools, LnkParse3, dnfile' -- all three are now present (LnkParse3 + dnfile in .venv).\"}\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"media-image-as-video-stream\", \"concept\": \"Still images asked through `media.*` (ffprobe opens JPEG/PNG/GIF/BMP/WebP as one video stream)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUG\n  {\"id\": \"video-geometry-crop-aspect\", \"concept\": \"Crop / aspect / display geometry of the primary video stream\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 flavor 'originals, crops'. fmt med\n  {\"id\": \"tnef-winmail\", \"concept\": \"TNEF winmail.dat attachments\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt tnef (alias winmail): signature_u32_hex (0x223e9f78), key_u16, message_class, at\n  {\"id\": \"pcap-header\", \"concept\": \"PCAP/PCAPNG global header, linktype, packet count, interfaces\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt pcap / pcapng, fields magic_u32_hex, version, li\n  {\"id\": \"macho-header\", \"concept\": \"Mach-O cputype/filetype/ncmds/LC_UUID\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt macho).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"rtf-onenote\", \"concept\": \"RTF \\\\objdata OLE1 objects, OneNote embedded files\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt rtf: object_class_names, object_count, template_target, inf\n  {\"id\": \"msitools-path\", \"concept\": \"msitools present but not on PATH\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"tools/msitools/usr/bin/{msiinfo,msidump,msiextract,gcab} exist but `source bin/env.\n]\n```","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a884a1e-870c-4737-be83-7e1c4a09a9ca","uuid":"9cb43845-c9db-4013-8bdd-c14655ed973b","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:04:23.594Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Readiness gaps\n\nRanking (D18 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D19-D21 question with no extractor (or a wrong-answer bug in an existing one), or a harness blocker that silently fails a\nwhole family of prebuilds. TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild 