{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBeN97BvzmFfcBMxXR1b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UnFm7PMw9YVG9ECVwpFSJQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md","content":"# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-19; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- Every day = ONE evidence zip (plain Deflate, no password so far). D1-7: one tiny member, ONE structural fact. D8-9:\n  the cumulative kit, every field in every mode. D10-14: one member + one field everywhere. **D15+ split the modes**:\n  single = 1 field (the new member), TT = cumulative kit (D15 20 -> D19 24 fields, +1 per day = the day's new member),\n  Mastery = 5 kits x the TT set, incl. a cross-member \"synthesis\" question every day. Pre-arm EVERY earlier family AND\n  the synthesis before the timed run; the timed field set is not the single's.\n- Member families: note/text -> jpg -> png -> pdf -> inner zip -> Go PE (D9-11) -> .NET dll (D12) -> MSI (D13) -> LNK\n  (D14) -> OOXML `.docx` (D15) -> `.eml` (D16) -> RIFF/WAVE audio (D17) -> MP4 h264+aac video (D18) -> Linux ELF (D19).\n  The fmt word is sometimes an ABSTRACT namespace (`email` not `eml`; `media` for BOTH audio D17 and video D18, with\n  ffprobe vocabulary) and sometimes the plain format (`elf` D19, like `pe`/`msi`/`lnk`) -- read it, never guess it.\n- A new `<fmt>.<field>` each day: identity -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` -> `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` ->\n  `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries` -> `zip.central_directory_member_names`\n  -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` -> `pe.version_original_filename` ->\n  `dotnet.mvid_guid` -> `msi.product_code_guid` -> `lnk.target_path_windows` -> `ooxml.external_relationship_targets` ->\n  `email.message_id` -> `media.primary_audio_codec_name` -> `media.primary_video_dimensions` -> `elf.e_machine_u16_hex`.\n  The question names the field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); ids `dNN-<family>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_`\n  -> `-`); `dNN` = the family's first day; `<family>` != `<fmt>` for media (`d17-audio-001-media-`, `d18-video-...`).\n- The flavor text promises extra findings (\"the collision\", \"the impossible destination\", \"equivalent recordings\",\n  \"crops ... the claimed device\", D19 \"Linux binaries from several systems ... rebuild deployment groups\") that were\n  NEVER asked; the sample usually delivers less (D9 \"several architectures\" -> one i386 PE; D19 \"several systems\" -> one\n  x86-64 ELF). The graded field is the STRUCTURAL truth from header bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the\n  lie. Pre-arm siblings without guessing spellings. Titles are puns (D19 \"Little Endian\" = ELF EI_DATA byte order).\n- Singles: D1-9 first-submit CORRECT ~27-60 s; D10, D13, D15 lost ONE submit to a convention (padding, braces, list\n  order); D16 lost TWO (parser -> `none`, stripped brackets); D17 ~24 s; D18 ~5 s and D19 ~13 s (race probe answered\n  from the prebuilt `lib.meta` registry before any LLM work). TT/Mastery: CORRECT every day, but D15-D17 AND D19 only\n  after an offline generalize (synthesis dispatch missing from the day's solver); D18 in-window first try.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\". Container NAMES drift: D1-14 `metadata-day-NN-evidence[-0N].zip`;\n  D15-19 TT `evidence.zip`, Mastery `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..05.zip`. Route by the ref's text before\n  `->` and by sha256, never a hard-coded name.\n- **Field-set size** -- per mode: D7 TT 11 / Mastery 22; D8-9 12-13 everywhere; D10-14 one; D15 1/20/100; D16 1/21/105;\n  D17 1/22/110; D18 1/23/115; D19 1/24/120. Families: identity + `d04-jpeg-*`, `d05-png-*`, `d06-pdf-*`, `d07-zip-*`\n  (eocd + CD names), `d09-pe-*` (machine, entry RVA, OriginalFilename), `d12-dotnet-*`, `d13-msi-*`, `d14-lnk-*`,\n  `d15-ooxml-*`, `d16-email-*`, `d17-audio-*`, `d18-video-*`, `d19-elf-*` + synthesis. Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX\n  (reference solver answering all 24: `challenges/day19/metadata-little-endian-on-the-prairie/solver/solve.py`).\n- **fmt word vs registry key vs id family word** (D16-D19) -- D16 `email.*` (prebuilt said `eml`); D17\n  `media.primary_audio_codec_name` id `d17-audio-...`; D18 `media.primary_video_dimensions` id `d18-video-...` (one\n  `media` namespace spans two families); D19 plain `elf.e_machine_u16_hex` id `d19-elf-001-elf-e-machine-u16-hex`\n  (family = fmt; spec name `e_machine` keeps its own underscore -> `e-machine`). Vocabulary = the field's home tool\n  (ffprobe for media) or the spec struct (`e_machine`, `coff_machine`). Rule: take `<fmt>.<field>` from the QUESTION\n  text (or the slug after `-NNN-`), map fmt synonyms (`email`<->`eml`/`mime`; `media`<->`audio`/`video`/`av`/...),\n  route the extractor by the member's MAGIC, fall back to the same field under any fmt.\n- **Identity member roster** (D15+) -- THREE small text members (`evidence-note.txt` 33 B, `evidence-note-copy.txt`\n  33 B, `roster.csv` 29 B); EACH identity question picks one at random per set: ids `<member-stem>-{filename,size-bytes,\n  md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}`. The filename question's artifact = the container only\n  (\"the exact filename of the roster\") -> map the id stem to the member. Never assume `evidence-note-*`.\n- **Synthesis / cross-member** (D15+) -- id `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<algo>-order` (TODAY's NN), kind `json`, norm\n  `case_insensitive`: \"Compute the full-file SHA-256 digest of each named file, then submit a compact JSON array of\n  their filenames in ascending digest order. Files: [...]\". The `artifact` names ONE member; the inputs are the\n  `Files:` list, same container. Rule: regex `Files:\\s*(\\[.*?\\])`, resolve each under the ref's container,\n  `hashlib.new(algo)` over raw bytes, sort by hex digest (descending only if said), emit names --\n  `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo)`, get_bytes bound to the artifacts root INSIDE the per-set\n  worker. Shape: note + 2 re-picked kit members (jpg/exe/docx D15, png/dll D17, png/msi D18, pdf/lnk D19) + TODAY's\n  member; order re-rolls per set. Only sha256 seen so far -- expect md5/sha1/size/time/arch-group siblings.\n- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree with the\n  header: answer from the structural bytes of the member the question names. D19 kit pools `collector-001.elf` with\n  `MZ` members (`telemetry-agent-001.exe`, `managed-001.dll`): an `elf.*` field of a non-ELF = literal `none`.\n- **Member values** -- re-roll per variant; never cache across sets. Seen re-rolled: note case id; D7 entry count\n  2-5; jpg/png dims per set (423x1089, 1255x1059); D10 entry RVA; D11 PE arch (0x014c/0x8664/0xaa64, OriginalFilename\n  `pe-base-<goarch>.exe` follows); D12 MVID; synthesis order. Constant so far (don't rely on it): D13 ProductCode,\n  D14 lnk target, D15 docx targets, kit exe/dll/msi/lnk, D17 codec `pcm_s16le`, D18 video `320x180`, D19 ELF (the same\n  14 408-B x86-64 LSB ELF64 ET_EXEC in single, TT and all 5 Mastery sets) -- the flavors' transcodes/crops/\"several\n  systems\" (big-endian MIPS/PPC, ARM, i386) are still due: read every ELF field with the file's own EI_CLASS/EI_DATA.\n- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes case-insensitive; `0x`-hex is `trim` only -> lowercase),\n  `enum` (`accepted_values`), `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact values and order\"). Emit per kind; read\n  `syntax` for prefix/case. JSON ORDER is field-specific -- see conventions.\n- **Question-text tags** -- D9 timed: ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<64 hex>]` suffix; D15+ timed: ``Inspect `<member>`. ``\n  prefix. Strip both before reading names; route by id + `artifact`.\n- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer\n  from an enclosing zip. An OOXML member is itself a zip -- parse it as the asked member, not as a wrapper to descend.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | python `zipfile` read of the member in memory (`7z l -slt` for orientation) |\n| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the member bytes; the id stem names WHICH member |\n| \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |\n| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`) -> `true`/`false` |\n| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width |\n| `png.ihdr_*` | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n| `zip.eocd_*` | of the NAMED zip: last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+10 total entries, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 (`PK\\x06\\x07` -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32) |\n| `zip.central_directory_*` | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from cd offset: name len @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name @+46. Raw stored path, CD order, no dedupe/sort; UTF-8 if flag 0x800 else UTF-8-then-cp437 |\n| `pdf.header_version` | `head -c 16 f | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; catalog `/Version` is a diagnostic only |\n| `pe.coff_*` | `MZ` -> e_lfanew u32 @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` -> Machine u16 @+4; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b`/`0x20b`) |\n| `pe.address_of_entry_point_*` / `pe.image_base*` | opt = e_lfanew+24: AddressOfEntryPoint u32 @opt+16 (RVA); ImageBase @opt+28 (PE32) / u64 @opt+24 (PE32+). objdump \"start address\" is the VA |\n| `pe.version_*` | `pefile` resource dir only -> `FileInfo..StringTable..entries`; id tail -> key ignoring case/`-_`. Shell: `strings -e l f.exe \\| grep -A1 OriginalFilename` |\n| `elf.*` (`7f 45 4c 46`) | EI_CLASS @4 (1=32, 2=64), EI_DATA @5 (1=LSB `<`, 2=MSB `>`) picks the struct byte order for EVERYTHING after @16: e_type u16 @16, e_machine u16 @18, e_version u32 @20, e_entry @24 (u32/u64 by class). `xxd -s 16 -l 4 f` + `readelf -h f`. In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `elf` (~45 fields: ei_*, e_type, e_entry_hex, e_flags, interp, build-id, section names). D19 `3e 00` LSB -> `0x003e` |\n| `macho.*` (promised, not yet asked) | `feedface`/`feedfacf` (BE) or `cefaedfe`/`cffaedfe` (LE) cputype u32 @4; fat `cafebabe` BE nfat_arch @4 (Java class shares the magic: major version @6 >= 45). `lib.meta` fmt `macho` |\n| `dotnet.*` / Mono assembly | data dir 14 -> CLI header -> `BSJB` -> `#~` (HeapSizes @+6, Valid @+8, rows @+24) -> Module row 0 Mvid (1-based #GUID idx) -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..)`. `lib/meta/dotnet.py` |\n| `msi.*` / `.msi` (OLE `d0 cf 11 e0`) | fast: `strings -n 6 x.msi \\| grep -aoE 'ProductCode\\{[0-9A-F-]{36}\\}'`; exact: CFB streams -> `!_StringPool`/`!_StringData` -> `!Property` (column-major). `olefile` in venv; `day13/.../solve.py msi_property` |\n| `lnk.*` / `.lnk` (`4c 00 00 00` + CLSID 00021401) | LinkFlags @0x14 (0x1 IDList, 0x2 LinkInfo, 0x80 Unicode); target = LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+CommonPathSuffix) verbatim, else IDList. `lib.meta.lnk:target_path` |\n| `ooxml.*` / `.docx/.xlsx/.pptx` (`PK` + `[Content_Types].xml`) | zip of XML parts. Relationships live in EVERY `*.rels` part. External = `TargetMode=\"External\"` (case-insensitive; absent = Internal). `unzip -p f.docx '*.rels' \\| grep -o 'Target=\"[^\"]*\" TargetMode=\"External\"'`; solver: `zipfile` + ElementTree over every `.rels`, local-name `Relationship` |\n| `email.*` / `.eml` (text `From:`/`Message-ID:`/`MIME-Version:`, CRLF) | `grep -ai '^message-id' f.eml`; solver: `lib.meta.prebuilt.eml.eml_value(data, {\"field\": f})` (stdlib `email`, unfolded raw header). Values VERBATIM (Message-ID keeps `<...>`). Threading = `In-Reply-To`/`References`/`Message-ID` |\n| `media.*` / audio (`RIFF..WAVE`, `ID3`/`ff fb`, `OggS`, `fLaC`, `ftyp`, `1a 45 df a3`, `FORM..AIFF`, `#!AMR`) | route by MAGIC. WAV: RIFF chunks from @12 to `fmt ` -> wFormatTag u16 @+8, bits u16 @+22 (0xFFFE -> SubFormat GUID first u16 @+32) -> FFmpeg names (Conventions). Truth: `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2 -hide_banner -i f` (no ffprobe; `mediainfo` says `PCM` = wrong vocabulary). In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `media`/`audio`/`av` |\n| `media.*video*` / MP4-MOV (`....ftyp`), MKV/WebM, AVI | box walk `moov` -> first `trak` whose `mdia/hdlr` = `vide` -> `stsd` entry: w,h u16 BE @entry+32; cross-check tkhd w/h + matrix, `pasp`, `clap`, SPS crop (may DISAGREE in a variant). In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `media`/`video` (`prebuilt/media_video.py`). Truth: bundled `ffmpeg -i` -> `Video: h264 (High) ..., 320x180 [SAR 1:1 DAR 16:9]` |\n| `*-synthesis-<algo>-order` / \"Files: [...]\" in the question | parse the list from the question text, hash each member of the same container, sort by digest, compact JSON of names |\n| GUID field (`*-guid`) | spelling follows the SOURCE: stored string (MSI) verbatim braces+uppercase; binary (.NET) -> lowercase, no braces |\n| exe-extension decoy (`MZ` without `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit |\n| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\", \"pooled with ... renamed data\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)`; decide ORDER per field (conventions) |\n| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids | resolve each set's container separately; see delivery layouts |\n\n## Day by day\n**Days 1-14** (one field each, all timed first try): D1 identity -> D2 `magic-prefix-hex-16` -> D3 BOM -> D4 JPEG SOFn\n`<w>x<h>` -> D5 PNG IHDR -> D6 `pdf.header_version` `x.y` -> D7 `zip.eocd_total_entries` of the INNER zip -> D8 CD names\n(compact JSON, CD order) -> D9-11 one Go PE: `coff_machine_u16_hex` `0x014c`, entry RVA `0x%08x` (unpadded REJECTED),\n`version_original_filename` verbatim -> D12 `dotnet.mvid_guid` (`uuid.UUID(bytes_le)` lowercase, no braces) -> D13\n`msi.product_code_guid` (stored WITH braces; brace-less REJECTED) -> D14 `lnk.target_path_windows` (LinkInfo path).\n\n**Days 15-18** (single = 1 new-family field; TT/Mastery = cumulative kit + synthesis): D15 \"A Word to the Wise\"\n`ooxml.external_relationship_targets` (`.docx` rels `TargetMode=\"External\"` -> Targets SORTED; rels order REJECTED,\n+50 s). D16 \"Return to Sender\" `email.message_id` (VERBATIM with `<>`; lost 2 submits: id regex hit the first `email-`\n-> `none`, then stripped brackets). D17 \"Hear Me Out\" `media.primary_audio_codec_name` (RIFF PCM 16-bit mono -> ffprobe\nname `pcm_s16le`, not `PCM`/`0x0001`; ~24 s). D18 \"Frame of Reference\" `media.primary_video_dimensions` (`video-001.mp4`\nh264 High + aac; first `vide` trak's stsd w x h = `320x180`, lowercase `x`; the audio trak must not be picked; race\nprobe answered from prebuilt `media_video.py` in ~5 s). D15-D17 timed: `synthesis-sha256-order` missing from the day's\ntemplate -> `solver_incomplete` -> offline generalize -> CORRECT. D18: the single worker pre-wired the synthesis ->\nTT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try.\n\n**Day 19 — Little Endian on the Prairie** (`elf.e_machine_u16_hex`, kind `pattern` \"lowercase hexadecimal with a 0x\nprefix and no explanatory text\", norm `trim`, id `d19-elf-001-elf-e-machine-u16-hex`). Prompt: \"Linux binaries from\nseveral systems have been pooled with Windows executables and renamed data. Determine architecture directly from the\nELF header and rebuild deployment groups.\" (several systems / renamed data / deployment groups -- NOT asked).\n- Artifact: 1 849-B zip -> `collector-001.elf` (14 408 B): ELF64 (EI_CLASS 2) LSB (EI_DATA 1), OSABI 0 SYSV, ET_EXEC\n  (2), x86-64, dynamically linked, PT_INTERP `/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2`, `.note.ABI-tag` GNU/Linux 3.2.0, stripped,\n  no `.note.gnu.build-id`. Bytes @18 = `3e 00`.\n- Key insight: the title pun IS the field rule -- read e_machine with the byte order EI_DATA declares (`<H` here, `>H`\n  for MSB MIPS/PPC/s390x/SPARC), then spell it like D9's `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`: `0x` + 4 lowercase zero-padded\n  digits = `0x003e` (not `0x3e`, not `x86-64`/`EM_X86_64`/`62`). Common values: i386 `0x0003`, SPARC `0x0002`, MIPS\n  `0x0008`, PPC `0x0014`, PPC64 `0x0015`, s390 `0x0016`, ARM `0x0028`, SPARCV9 `0x002b`, x86-64 `0x003e`, AArch64\n  `0x00b7`, RISC-V `0x00f3`, LoongArch `0x0102`.\n- Tools: none by hand -- the race probe answered from `lib.meta` fmt `elf` (D18-night `elf-header` prebuild; tier still\n  `speculative`; a synthesized MSB MIPS header answers `0x0008`, a PE/text member `none`). Manual: `xxd -s 4 -l 2 f`\n  (class, data) + `xxd -s 18 -l 2 f`; `readelf -h f` \"Machine: Advanced Micro Devices X86-64\".\n- Single CORRECT on the first submit ~13 s after start (race transport 3.1 s). The single worker then added an explicit\n  endian-aware extractor to `solve.py` but NOT the synthesis dispatch -> TT (24 fields; 23 verified in-window 6.0 s)\n  and Mastery (120; 115 verified in-window 6.0 s) both `solver_incomplete` on `metadata-day-19-synthesis-sha256-order`\n  (Files: note + `document-001.pdf` + `shortcut-001.lnk` + `collector-001.elf`) -> generalize ported D18's\n  `synthesis-<algo>-order` branch (+ `_ROOT` set inside `_solve_pairs`) -> TT CORRECT (2 generalize workers),\n  Mastery CORRECT (1). Same failure as D15-D17: the regression was the template, not the parse.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`). Booleans: enum `true` / `false`.\n- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR, video `media.primary_video_dimensions` D18): `<width>x<height>`, lowercase\n  `x`, no spaces. Video = ffprobe width/height of v:0 (coded size, NOT rotated, not the tkhd display size).\n- PDF header version: bare `x.y`; absent -> literal `none` (wording; `none` not yet GM-confirmed). Counts: plain integer.\n- JSON lists -- compact, double quotes, no spaces; ORDER depends on the field:\n  - `zip.central_directory_member_names`: full stored paths in CD order (`[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]`).\n  - `ooxml.external_relationship_targets`: Target strings SORTED ascending (D15 all modes); rels-file order REJECTED.\n  - `*-synthesis-<algo>-order`: member names ordered by hex digest ascending (D15-D19 TT/Mastery; `case_insensitive`).\n  Heuristic: a list read off one on-disk structure that the field name calls \"names in the directory\" keeps disk\n  order; a set gathered across parts (\"targets\", \"dependencies\") is sorted. If an order is rejected, try the other.\n- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 PE Machine\n  `0x014c`, u16 ELF e_machine `0x003e` (D19), u32 AddressOfEntryPoint `0x00065bd0`. Width from the STRUCT / the\n  `_uNN_` in the id; the value from the file's own byte order (ELF EI_DATA). (Magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; the\n  binary lane's machine wants `i386` and accepted unpadded entry points -- different generator.)\n- GUIDs: .NET MVID `Guid.ToString()` lowercase no braces (D12); MSI ProductCode the stored string uppercase WITH braces\n  (D13). Spelling follows the source, not answer_format.\n- Windows paths (`lnk.target_path_windows`): stored LinkInfo path verbatim (backslashes, case, drive letter, no quotes).\n- Version-resource strings (`pe.version_<field>`): StringFileInfo value verbatim incl. extension.\n- URLs (`ooxml` Targets): the attribute value verbatim -- scheme, host, path as stored; no trailing-slash or case fixups.\n- E-mail headers (`email.<field>`): header value as stored after RFC 5322 unfolding; Message-ID WITH `<>` (D16).\n- Media codec names (`media.*codec_name`, D17): FFmpeg/ffprobe `codec_name`, lowercase: WAV tag 1 -> `pcm_u8` (8-bit) /\n  `pcm_s16le` / `pcm_s24le` / `pcm_s32le` (RIFX -> `..be`); tag 3 -> `pcm_f32le`/`pcm_f64le`; 6 `pcm_alaw`; 7\n  `pcm_mulaw`; 2 `adpcm_ms`; 0x11 `adpcm_ima_wav`; 0x55 `mp3`; 0xFFFE -> SubFormat GUID first u16. Others: `mp3`, `aac`,\n  `opus`, `vorbis`, `flac`, `alac`, `amr_nb`/`amr_wb`, `ac3`. Only `pcm_s16le` is GM-verified.\n- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` (D10, unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-file-order target list (D15);\n  bracket-less Message-ID (D16). Pattern: delimiters that are part of the stored value (`{}`, `<>`) stay.\n- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_` = SOF header, `eocd_total_entries` = the EOCD's own claim,\n  `e_machine` = Elf_Ehdr member) -- read it literally to pick the structure. A claimed count is NOT a CD walk; CD\n  names are NOT local-header names; `_uNN_hex` fixes read+print width. Unverified ELF siblings: bare enum-ish fields\n  (`ei_data`, `e_type`) have no GM spelling yet -- lib emits `ELFDATA2LSB` / `2`; prefer the `_hex` form if offered.\n\n## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (filename questions: artifact = the zip only).\n- Mastery zip-of-zips (days 1,2,4,5,7,8,10,11,14,15-19): ONE download (`...-evidence-01.zip`; D15+ `evidence-01.zip`)\n  holding `-01.zip`..`-0N.zip`, each holding its set's member(s) (D7 three levels; D8/D15+ five full kits). Refs\n  `<set zip> -> <member>`; every set reuses member names -> resolve by (set zip, member).\n- Mastery day 9: download named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip` while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip` ->\n  resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not its filename.\n- Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` refs.\n- Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) -- never hardcode names.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Synthesis dispatch lost AGAIN (D15, D16, D17, D19)**: every day the single's `solve.py` answers the new field but the\n  timed kit adds `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-sha256-order` -> `solver_incomplete` -> an offline generalize (~1 min per\n  mode). D18 was clean only because the single worker pre-wired it. Right after single CORRECT: `grep -n synthesis\n  solver/solve.py` must show a dispatch calling `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order`, with the artifacts root set INSIDE\n  the per-set worker (`_solve_pairs`; Mastery forks one process per set), plus identity for ANY member stem and every\n  carry-over family. Start from the previous day's solver, not a fresh template.\n- Id-slug parsing (D16, 1 wrong): ids repeat the fmt word (`d16-email-001-email-message-id`); a regex on the first\n  `email-` yields `001-email-message-id` -> lookup miss -> `none`. Anchor `-\\d+-<fmt>-(.+)$`. Never submit `none`\n  without grepping the bytes for the field -- `none` means absent in the artifact, not \"my parser returned None\".\n- Registry misses (D14 key one suffix short `lnk.target_path`; D16 fmt `eml` vs GM `email`; D17 `wav.*` vs `media.*`):\n  `python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print([k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'])\"` and grep\n  `lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` for the FIELD name; call the nearest extractor directly before writing one. D18 (`media`)\n  and D19 (`elf`) both HIT the prebuilt registry -> answered in the race probe.\n- Endianness (D19 pun): never `struct.unpack('<H')` an ELF/Mach-O field blindly -- EI_DATA (ELF @5) / the Mach-O magic\n  byte order decide; ELF32 vs ELF64 moves every offset after e_version (e_entry/e_phoff/e_shoff widths).\n- Video geometry has FOUR sources (D18 they agreed; \"crops / impossible device\" flavor says variants won't): stsd\n  sample-entry w/h, codec SPS (h264 frame_cropping -> ffprobe `width`/`height`), tkhd 16.16 display w/h, tkhd matrix\n  rotation (ffprobe keeps coded dims). If a variant's stsd and SPS disagree, trust the SPS-cropped size, note it.\n- Field suffix picks the spelling: `_u16_hex` = the raw struct value (D9: not `i386`/GOARCH; D19: not `x86-64`);\n  `_codec_name` = the tool vocabulary (D17: `pcm_s16le`, not the raw format tag `1` nor mediainfo's `PCM`).\n- JSON list ORDER (D15, 1 wrong + ~26 s): \"exact values and order\" does not say WHICH order. File order was rejected\n  for rels targets; sorted won. Decide per field (conventions above) before the first submit.\n- Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (D2 TT); a pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the 409\n  `start_required` body (questions, NO `answer_ids`). Answer under the live `answer_ids`.\n- Don't let the flavor text widen the question: only the named field is graded; extra checks are diagnostics.\n- Container-of-containers: a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded zip reads the OUTER EOCD, a name lookup on\n  zip-of-zips returned `PK` as the \"magic\". Resolve the named member's bytes first (recurse), then parse.\n- Name-list fields: emit CD bytes as-is for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `\\`, dupes). Decoy names (`*-with-bom.txt`,\n  `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF): bytes win every time.\n- Timed windows are seconds; most of it is GM round-trips (D19 start 2.4-2.8 s + download 2.7-3.2 s + submit 1.9 s;\n  solve ~1 s). Parse in memory, never shell out/extract to disk in-window; decompress each member once, cache by\n  (set zip, member).\n- Normalizing a stored value (D13): don't strip braces/reshape a stored string because answer_format sounds generic.\n- Hex width (D10): `\"0x%x\"` drops leading zeros; print `0x%0{2*size}x`. `_rva` = raw field, never ImageBase + it.\n  Require `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew before any PE field; require `\\x7fELF` before any ELF field.\n- Harness: `hctf start` on a solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` (D2) -- restore from `log.jsonl`.\n- Tools installed: exiftool, poppler, qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck, zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost,\n  mediainfo, sqlite3, ImageMagick, readelf/objdump, olevba/oleid, olefile, pefile, pyelftools, LnkParse3, dnfile,\n  mutagen (.venv); msitools under tools/msitools; ffmpeg 7.0.2 (no ffprobe) at\n  `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2` (not on PATH). NOT installed: ffprobe, sox.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1784,"cache_read_input_tokens":92136,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1784},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a884a1e-870c-4737-be83-7e1c4a09a9ca","uuid":"5e956af3-9b26-4e57-b484-9250c144f510","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:07:19.049Z","request_id":"req_011CgBeN8kMvYVmkQ29iknTs","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UnFm7PMw9YVG9ECVwpFSJQ":{"file_path":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md","content":"# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-19; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- Every day = ONE evidence zip (plain Deflate, no password so far). D1-7: one tiny member, ONE structural fact. D8-9:\n  the cumulative kit, every field in every mode. D10-14: one member + one field everywhere. **D15+ split the modes**:\n  single = 1 field (the new member), TT = cumulative kit (D15 20 -> D19 24 fields, +1 per day = the day's new member),\n  Mastery = 5 kits x the TT set, incl. a cross-member \"synthesis\" question every day. Pre-arm EVERY earlier family AND\n  the synthesis before the timed run; the timed field set is not the single's.\n- Member families: note/text -> jpg -> png -> pdf -> inner zip -> Go PE (D9-11) -> .NET dll (D12) -> MSI (D13) -> LNK\n  (D14) -> OOXML `.docx` (D15) -> `.eml` (D16) -> RIFF/WAVE audio (D17) -> MP4 h264+aac video (D18) -> Linux ELF (D19).\n  The fmt word is sometimes an ABSTRACT namespace (`email` not `eml`; `media` for BOTH audio D17 and video D18, with\n  ffprobe vocabulary) and sometimes the plain format (`elf` D19, like `pe`/`msi`/`lnk`) -- read it, never guess it.\n- A new `<fmt>.<field>` each day: identity -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` -> `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` ->\n  `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries` -> `zip.central_directory_member_names`\n  -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` -> `pe.version_original_filename` ->\n  `dotnet.mvid_guid` -> `msi.product_code_guid` -> `lnk.target_path_windows` -> `ooxml.external_relationship_targets` ->\n  `email.message_id` -> `media.primary_audio_codec_name` -> `media.primary_video_dimensions` -> `elf.e_machine_u16_hex`.\n  The question names the field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); ids `dNN-<family>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_`\n  -> `-`); `dNN` = the family's first day; `<family>` != `<fmt>` for media (`d17-audio-001-media-`, `d18-video-...`).\n- The flavor text promises extra findings (\"the collision\", \"the impossible destination\", \"equivalent recordings\",\n  \"crops ... the claimed device\", D19 \"Linux binaries from several systems ... rebuild deployment groups\") that were\n  NEVER asked; the sample usually delivers less (D9 \"several architectures\" -> one i386 PE; D19 \"several systems\" -> one\n  x86-64 ELF). The graded field is the STRUCTURAL truth from header bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the\n  lie. Pre-arm siblings without guessing spellings. Titles are puns (D19 \"Little Endian\" = ELF EI_DATA byte order).\n- Singles: D1-9 first-submit CORRECT ~27-60 s; D10, D13, D15 lost ONE submit to a convention (padding, braces, list\n  order); D16 lost TWO (parser -> `none`, stripped brackets); D17 ~24 s; D18 ~5 s and D19 ~13 s (race probe answered\n  from the prebuilt `lib.meta` registry before any LLM work). TT/Mastery: CORRECT every day, but D15-D17 AND D19 only\n  after an offline generalize (synthesis dispatch missing from the day's solver); D18 in-window first try.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\". Container NAMES drift: D1-14 `metadata-day-NN-evidence[-0N].zip`;\n  D15-19 TT `evidence.zip`, Mastery `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..05.zip`. Route by the ref's text before\n  `->` and by sha256, never a hard-coded name.\n- **Field-set size** -- per mode: D7 TT 11 / Mastery 22; D8-9 12-13 everywhere; D10-14 one; D15 1/20/100; D16 1/21/105;\n  D17 1/22/110; D18 1/23/115; D19 1/24/120. Families: identity + `d04-jpeg-*`, `d05-png-*`, `d06-pdf-*`, `d07-zip-*`\n  (eocd + CD names), `d09-pe-*` (machine, entry RVA, OriginalFilename), `d12-dotnet-*`, `d13-msi-*`, `d14-lnk-*`,\n  `d15-ooxml-*`, `d16-email-*`, `d17-audio-*`, `d18-video-*`, `d19-elf-*` + synthesis. Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX\n  (reference solver answering all 24: `challenges/day19/metadata-little-endian-on-the-prairie/solver/solve.py`).\n- **fmt word vs registry key vs id family word** (D16-D19) -- D16 `email.*` (prebuilt said `eml`); D17\n  `media.primary_audio_codec_name` id `d17-audio-...`; D18 `media.primary_video_dimensions` id `d18-video-...` (one\n  `media` namespace spans two families); D19 plain `elf.e_machine_u16_hex` id `d19-elf-001-elf-e-machine-u16-hex`\n  (family = fmt; spec name `e_machine` keeps its own underscore -> `e-machine`). Vocabulary = the field's home tool\n  (ffprobe for media) or the spec struct (`e_machine`, `coff_machine`). Rule: take `<fmt>.<field>` from the QUESTION\n  text (or the slug after `-NNN-`), map fmt synonyms (`email`<->`eml`/`mime`; `media`<->`audio`/`video`/`av`/...),\n  route the extractor by the member's MAGIC, fall back to the same field under any fmt.\n- **Identity member roster** (D15+) -- THREE small text members (`evidence-note.txt` 33 B, `evidence-note-copy.txt`\n  33 B, `roster.csv` 29 B); EACH identity question picks one at random per set: ids `<member-stem>-{filename,size-bytes,\n  md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}`. The filename question's artifact = the container only\n  (\"the exact filename of the roster\") -> map the id stem to the member. Never assume `evidence-note-*`.\n- **Synthesis / cross-member** (D15+) -- id `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<algo>-order` (TODAY's NN), kind `json`, norm\n  `case_insensitive`: \"Compute the full-file SHA-256 digest of each named file, then submit a compact JSON array of\n  their filenames in ascending digest order. Files: [...]\". The `artifact` names ONE member; the inputs are the\n  `Files:` list, same container. Rule: regex `Files:\\s*(\\[.*?\\])`, resolve each under the ref's container,\n  `hashlib.new(algo)` over raw bytes, sort by hex digest (descending only if said), emit names --\n  `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo)`, get_bytes bound to the artifacts root INSIDE the per-set\n  worker. Shape: note + 2 re-picked kit members (jpg/exe/docx D15, png/dll D17, png/msi D18, pdf/lnk D19) + TODAY's\n  member; order re-rolls per set. Only sha256 seen so far -- expect md5/sha1/size/time/arch-group siblings.\n- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree with the\n  header: answer from the structural bytes of the member the question names. D19 kit pools `collector-001.elf` with\n  `MZ` members (`telemetry-agent-001.exe`, `managed-001.dll`): an `elf.*` field of a non-ELF = literal `none`.\n- **Member values** -- re-roll per variant; never cache across sets. Seen re-rolled: note case id; D7 entry count\n  2-5; jpg/png dims per set (423x1089, 1255x1059); D10 entry RVA; D11 PE arch (0x014c/0x8664/0xaa64, OriginalFilename\n  `pe-base-<goarch>.exe` follows); D12 MVID; synthesis order. Constant so far (don't rely on it): D13 ProductCode,\n  D14 lnk target, D15 docx targets, kit exe/dll/msi/lnk, D17 codec `pcm_s16le`, D18 video `320x180`, D19 ELF (the same\n  14 408-B x86-64 LSB ELF64 ET_EXEC in single, TT and all 5 Mastery sets) -- the flavors' transcodes/crops/\"several\n  systems\" (big-endian MIPS/PPC, ARM, i386) are still due: read every ELF field with the file's own EI_CLASS/EI_DATA.\n- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes case-insensitive; `0x`-hex is `trim` only -> lowercase),\n  `enum` (`accepted_values`), `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact values and order\"). Emit per kind; read\n  `syntax` for prefix/case. JSON ORDER is field-specific -- see conventions.\n- **Question-text tags** -- D9 timed: ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<64 hex>]` suffix; D15+ timed: ``Inspect `<member>`. ``\n  prefix. Strip both before reading names; route by id + `artifact`.\n- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer\n  from an enclosing zip. An OOXML member is itself a zip -- parse it as the asked member, not as a wrapper to descend.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | python `zipfile` read of the member in memory (`7z l -slt` for orientation) |\n| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the member bytes; the id stem names WHICH member |\n| \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |\n| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`) -> `true`/`false` |\n| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width |\n| `png.ihdr_*` | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n| `zip.eocd_*` | of the NAMED zip: last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+10 total entries, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 (`PK\\x06\\x07` -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32) |\n| `zip.central_directory_*` | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from cd offset: name len @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name @+46. Raw stored path, CD order, no dedupe/sort; UTF-8 if flag 0x800 else UTF-8-then-cp437 |\n| `pdf.header_version` | `head -c 16 f | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; catalog `/Version` is a diagnostic only |\n| `pe.coff_*` | `MZ` -> e_lfanew u32 @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` -> Machine u16 @+4; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b`/`0x20b`) |\n| `pe.address_of_entry_point_*` / `pe.image_base*` | opt = e_lfanew+24: AddressOfEntryPoint u32 @opt+16 (RVA); ImageBase @opt+28 (PE32) / u64 @opt+24 (PE32+). objdump \"start address\" is the VA |\n| `pe.version_*` | `pefile` resource dir only -> `FileInfo..StringTable..entries`; id tail -> key ignoring case/`-_`. Shell: `strings -e l f.exe \\| grep -A1 OriginalFilename` |\n| `elf.*` (`7f 45 4c 46`) | EI_CLASS @4 (1=32, 2=64), EI_DATA @5 (1=LSB `<`, 2=MSB `>`) picks the struct byte order for EVERYTHING after @16: e_type u16 @16, e_machine u16 @18, e_version u32 @20, e_entry @24 (u32/u64 by class). `xxd -s 16 -l 4 f` + `readelf -h f`. In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `elf` (~45 fields: ei_*, e_type, e_entry_hex, e_flags, interp, build-id, section names). D19 `3e 00` LSB -> `0x003e` |\n| `macho.*` (promised, not yet asked) | `feedface`/`feedfacf` (BE) or `cefaedfe`/`cffaedfe` (LE) cputype u32 @4; fat `cafebabe` BE nfat_arch @4 (Java class shares the magic: major version @6 >= 45). `lib.meta` fmt `macho` |\n| `dotnet.*` / Mono assembly | data dir 14 -> CLI header -> `BSJB` -> `#~` (HeapSizes @+6, Valid @+8, rows @+24) -> Module row 0 Mvid (1-based #GUID idx) -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..)`. `lib/meta/dotnet.py` |\n| `msi.*` / `.msi` (OLE `d0 cf 11 e0`) | fast: `strings -n 6 x.msi \\| grep -aoE 'ProductCode\\{[0-9A-F-]{36}\\}'`; exact: CFB streams -> `!_StringPool`/`!_StringData` -> `!Property` (column-major). `olefile` in venv; `day13/.../solve.py msi_property` |\n| `lnk.*` / `.lnk` (`4c 00 00 00` + CLSID 00021401) | LinkFlags @0x14 (0x1 IDList, 0x2 LinkInfo, 0x80 Unicode); target = LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+CommonPathSuffix) verbatim, else IDList. `lib.meta.lnk:target_path` |\n| `ooxml.*` / `.docx/.xlsx/.pptx` (`PK` + `[Content_Types].xml`) | zip of XML parts. Relationships live in EVERY `*.rels` part. External = `TargetMode=\"External\"` (case-insensitive; absent = Internal). `unzip -p f.docx '*.rels' \\| grep -o 'Target=\"[^\"]*\" TargetMode=\"External\"'`; solver: `zipfile` + ElementTree over every `.rels`, local-name `Relationship` |\n| `email.*` / `.eml` (text `From:`/`Message-ID:`/`MIME-Version:`, CRLF) | `grep -ai '^message-id' f.eml`; solver: `lib.meta.prebuilt.eml.eml_value(data, {\"field\": f})` (stdlib `email`, unfolded raw header). Values VERBATIM (Message-ID keeps `<...>`). Threading = `In-Reply-To`/`References`/`Message-ID` |\n| `media.*` / audio (`RIFF..WAVE`, `ID3`/`ff fb`, `OggS`, `fLaC`, `ftyp`, `1a 45 df a3`, `FORM..AIFF`, `#!AMR`) | route by MAGIC. WAV: RIFF chunks from @12 to `fmt ` -> wFormatTag u16 @+8, bits u16 @+22 (0xFFFE -> SubFormat GUID first u16 @+32) -> FFmpeg names (Conventions). Truth: `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2 -hide_banner -i f` (no ffprobe; `mediainfo` says `PCM` = wrong vocabulary). In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `media`/`audio`/`av` |\n| `media.*video*` / MP4-MOV (`....ftyp`), MKV/WebM, AVI | box walk `moov` -> first `trak` whose `mdia/hdlr` = `vide` -> `stsd` entry: w,h u16 BE @entry+32; cross-check tkhd w/h + matrix, `pasp`, `clap`, SPS crop (may DISAGREE in a variant). In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `media`/`video` (`prebuilt/media_video.py`). Truth: bundled `ffmpeg -i` -> `Video: h264 (High) ..., 320x180 [SAR 1:1 DAR 16:9]` |\n| `*-synthesis-<algo>-order` / \"Files: [...]\" in the question | parse the list from the question text, hash each member of the same container, sort by digest, compact JSON of names |\n| GUID field (`*-guid`) | spelling follows the SOURCE: stored string (MSI) verbatim braces+uppercase; binary (.NET) -> lowercase, no braces |\n| exe-extension decoy (`MZ` without `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit |\n| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\", \"pooled with ... renamed data\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)`; decide ORDER per field (conventions) |\n| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids | resolve each set's container separately; see delivery layouts |\n\n## Day by day\n**Days 1-14** (one field each, all timed first try): D1 identity -> D2 `magic-prefix-hex-16` -> D3 BOM -> D4 JPEG SOFn\n`<w>x<h>` -> D5 PNG IHDR -> D6 `pdf.header_version` `x.y` -> D7 `zip.eocd_total_entries` of the INNER zip -> D8 CD names\n(compact JSON, CD order) -> D9-11 one Go PE: `coff_machine_u16_hex` `0x014c`, entry RVA `0x%08x` (unpadded REJECTED),\n`version_original_filename` verbatim -> D12 `dotnet.mvid_guid` (`uuid.UUID(bytes_le)` lowercase, no braces) -> D13\n`msi.product_code_guid` (stored WITH braces; brace-less REJECTED) -> D14 `lnk.target_path_windows` (LinkInfo path).\n\n**Days 15-18** (single = 1 new-family field; TT/Mastery = cumulative kit + synthesis): D15 \"A Word to the Wise\"\n`ooxml.external_relationship_targets` (`.docx` rels `TargetMode=\"External\"` -> Targets SORTED; rels order REJECTED,\n+50 s). D16 \"Return to Sender\" `email.message_id` (VERBATIM with `<>`; lost 2 submits: id regex hit the first `email-`\n-> `none`, then stripped brackets). D17 \"Hear Me Out\" `media.primary_audio_codec_name` (RIFF PCM 16-bit mono -> ffprobe\nname `pcm_s16le`, not `PCM`/`0x0001`; ~24 s). D18 \"Frame of Reference\" `media.primary_video_dimensions` (`video-001.mp4`\nh264 High + aac; first `vide` trak's stsd w x h = `320x180`, lowercase `x`; the audio trak must not be picked; race\nprobe answered from prebuilt `media_video.py` in ~5 s). D15-D17 timed: `synthesis-sha256-order` missing from the day's\ntemplate -> `solver_incomplete` -> offline generalize -> CORRECT. D18: the single worker pre-wired the synthesis ->\nTT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try.\n\n**Day 19 — Little Endian on the Prairie** (`elf.e_machine_u16_hex`, kind `pattern` \"lowercase hexadecimal with a 0x\nprefix and no explanatory text\", norm `trim`, id `d19-elf-001-elf-e-machine-u16-hex`). Prompt: \"Linux binaries from\nseveral systems have been pooled with Windows executables and renamed data. Determine architecture directly from the\nELF header and rebuild deployment groups.\" (several systems / renamed data / deployment groups -- NOT asked).\n- Artifact: 1 849-B zip -> `collector-001.elf` (14 408 B): ELF64 (EI_CLASS 2) LSB (EI_DATA 1), OSABI 0 SYSV, ET_EXEC\n  (2), x86-64, dynamically linked, PT_INTERP `/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2`, `.note.ABI-tag` GNU/Linux 3.2.0, stripped,\n  no `.note.gnu.build-id`. Bytes @18 = `3e 00`.\n- Key insight: the title pun IS the field rule -- read e_machine with the byte order EI_DATA declares (`<H` here, `>H`\n  for MSB MIPS/PPC/s390x/SPARC), then spell it like D9's `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`: `0x` + 4 lowercase zero-padded\n  digits = `0x003e` (not `0x3e`, not `x86-64`/`EM_X86_64`/`62`). Common values: i386 `0x0003`, SPARC `0x0002`, MIPS\n  `0x0008`, PPC `0x0014`, PPC64 `0x0015`, s390 `0x0016`, ARM `0x0028`, SPARCV9 `0x002b`, x86-64 `0x003e`, AArch64\n  `0x00b7`, RISC-V `0x00f3`, LoongArch `0x0102`.\n- Tools: none by hand -- the race probe answered from `lib.meta` fmt `elf` (D18-night `elf-header` prebuild; tier still\n  `speculative`; a synthesized MSB MIPS header answers `0x0008`, a PE/text member `none`). Manual: `xxd -s 4 -l 2 f`\n  (class, data) + `xxd -s 18 -l 2 f`; `readelf -h f` \"Machine: Advanced Micro Devices X86-64\".\n- Single CORRECT on the first submit ~13 s after start (race transport 3.1 s). The single worker then added an explicit\n  endian-aware extractor to `solve.py` but NOT the synthesis dispatch -> TT (24 fields; 23 verified in-window 6.0 s)\n  and Mastery (120; 115 verified in-window 6.0 s) both `solver_incomplete` on `metadata-day-19-synthesis-sha256-order`\n  (Files: note + `document-001.pdf` + `shortcut-001.lnk` + `collector-001.elf`) -> generalize ported D18's\n  `synthesis-<algo>-order` branch (+ `_ROOT` set inside `_solve_pairs`) -> TT CORRECT (2 generalize workers),\n  Mastery CORRECT (1). Same failure as D15-D17: the regression was the template, not the parse.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`). Booleans: enum `true` / `false`.\n- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR, video `media.primary_video_dimensions` D18): `<width>x<height>`, lowercase\n  `x`, no spaces. Video = ffprobe width/height of v:0 (coded size, NOT rotated, not the tkhd display size).\n- PDF header version: bare `x.y`; absent -> literal `none` (wording; `none` not yet GM-confirmed). Counts: plain integer.\n- JSON lists -- compact, double quotes, no spaces; ORDER depends on the field:\n  - `zip.central_directory_member_names`: full stored paths in CD order (`[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]`).\n  - `ooxml.external_relationship_targets`: Target strings SORTED ascending (D15 all modes); rels-file order REJECTED.\n  - `*-synthesis-<algo>-order`: member names ordered by hex digest ascending (D15-D19 TT/Mastery; `case_insensitive`).\n  Heuristic: a list read off one on-disk structure that the field name calls \"names in the directory\" keeps disk\n  order; a set gathered across parts (\"targets\", \"dependencies\") is sorted. If an order is rejected, try the other.\n- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 PE Machine\n  `0x014c`, u16 ELF e_machine `0x003e` (D19), u32 AddressOfEntryPoint `0x00065bd0`. Width from the STRUCT / the\n  `_uNN_` in the id; the value from the file's own byte order (ELF EI_DATA). (Magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; the\n  binary lane's machine wants `i386` and accepted unpadded entry points -- different generator.)\n- GUIDs: .NET MVID `Guid.ToString()` lowercase no braces (D12); MSI ProductCode the stored string uppercase WITH braces\n  (D13). Spelling follows the source, not answer_format.\n- Windows paths (`lnk.target_path_windows`): stored LinkInfo path verbatim (backslashes, case, drive letter, no quotes).\n- Version-resource strings (`pe.version_<field>`): StringFileInfo value verbatim incl. extension.\n- URLs (`ooxml` Targets): the attribute value verbatim -- scheme, host, path as stored; no trailing-slash or case fixups.\n- E-mail headers (`email.<field>`): header value as stored after RFC 5322 unfolding; Message-ID WITH `<>` (D16).\n- Media codec names (`media.*codec_name`, D17): FFmpeg/ffprobe `codec_name`, lowercase: WAV tag 1 -> `pcm_u8` (8-bit) /\n  `pcm_s16le` / `pcm_s24le` / `pcm_s32le` (RIFX -> `..be`); tag 3 -> `pcm_f32le`/`pcm_f64le`; 6 `pcm_alaw`; 7\n  `pcm_mulaw`; 2 `adpcm_ms`; 0x11 `adpcm_ima_wav`; 0x55 `mp3`; 0xFFFE -> SubFormat GUID first u16. Others: `mp3`, `aac`,\n  `opus`, `vorbis`, `flac`, `alac`, `amr_nb`/`amr_wb`, `ac3`. Only `pcm_s16le` is GM-verified.\n- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` (D10, unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-file-order target list (D15);\n  bracket-less Message-ID (D16). Pattern: delimiters that are part of the stored value (`{}`, `<>`) stay.\n- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_` = SOF header, `eocd_total_entries` = the EOCD's own claim,\n  `e_machine` = Elf_Ehdr member) -- read it literally to pick the structure. A claimed count is NOT a CD walk; CD\n  names are NOT local-header names; `_uNN_hex` fixes read+print width. Unverified ELF siblings: bare enum-ish fields\n  (`ei_data`, `e_type`) have no GM spelling yet -- lib emits `ELFDATA2LSB` / `2`; prefer the `_hex` form if offered.\n\n## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (filename questions: artifact = the zip only).\n- Mastery zip-of-zips (days 1,2,4,5,7,8,10,11,14,15-19): ONE download (`...-evidence-01.zip`; D15+ `evidence-01.zip`)\n  holding `-01.zip`..`-0N.zip`, each holding its set's member(s) (D7 three levels; D8/D15+ five full kits). Refs\n  `<set zip> -> <member>`; every set reuses member names -> resolve by (set zip, member).\n- Mastery day 9: download named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip` while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip` ->\n  resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not its filename.\n- Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` refs.\n- Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) -- never hardcode names.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Synthesis dispatch lost AGAIN (D15, D16, D17, D19)**: every day the single's `solve.py` answers the new field but the\n  timed kit adds `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-sha256-order` -> `solver_incomplete` -> an offline generalize (~1 min per\n  mode). D18 was clean only because the single worker pre-wired it. Right after single CORRECT: `grep -n synthesis\n  solver/solve.py` must show a dispatch calling `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order`, with the artifacts root set INSIDE\n  the per-set worker (`_solve_pairs`; Mastery forks one process per set), plus identity for ANY member stem and every\n  carry-over family. Start from the previous day's solver, not a fresh template.\n- Id-slug parsing (D16, 1 wrong): ids repeat the fmt word (`d16-email-001-email-message-id`); a regex on the first\n  `email-` yields `001-email-message-id` -> lookup miss -> `none`. Anchor `-\\d+-<fmt>-(.+)$`. Never submit `none`\n  without grepping the bytes for the field -- `none` means absent in the artifact, not \"my parser returned None\".\n- Registry misses (D14 key one suffix short `lnk.target_path`; D16 fmt `eml` vs GM `email`; D17 `wav.*` vs `media.*`):\n  `python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print([k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'])\"` and grep\n  `lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` for the FIELD name; call the nearest extractor directly before writing one. D18 (`media`)\n  and D19 (`elf`) both HIT the prebuilt registry -> answered in the race probe.\n- Endianness (D19 pun): never `struct.unpack('<H')` an ELF/Mach-O field blindly -- EI_DATA (ELF @5) / the Mach-O magic\n  byte order decide; ELF32 vs ELF64 moves every offset after e_version (e_entry/e_phoff/e_shoff widths).\n- Video geometry has FOUR sources (D18 they agreed; \"crops / impossible device\" flavor says variants won't): stsd\n  sample-entry w/h, codec SPS (h264 frame_cropping -> ffprobe `width`/`height`), tkhd 16.16 display w/h, tkhd matrix\n  rotation (ffprobe keeps coded dims). If a variant's stsd and SPS disagree, trust the SPS-cropped size, note it.\n- Field suffix picks the spelling: `_u16_hex` = the raw struct value (D9: not `i386`/GOARCH; D19: not `x86-64`);\n  `_codec_name` = the tool vocabulary (D17: `pcm_s16le`, not the raw format tag `1` nor mediainfo's `PCM`).\n- JSON list ORDER (D15, 1 wrong + ~26 s): \"exact values and order\" does not say WHICH order. File order was rejected\n  for rels targets; sorted won. Decide per field (conventions above) before the first submit.\n- Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (D2 TT); a pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the 409\n  `start_required` body (questions, NO `answer_ids`). Answer under the live `answer_ids`.\n- Don't let the flavor text widen the question: only the named field is graded; extra checks are diagnostics.\n- Container-of-containers: a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded zip reads the OUTER EOCD, a name lookup on\n  zip-of-zips returned `PK` as the \"magic\". Resolve the named member's bytes first (recurse), then parse.\n- Name-list fields: emit CD bytes as-is for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `\\`, dupes). Decoy names (`*-with-bom.txt`,\n  `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF): bytes win every time.\n- Timed windows are seconds; most of it is GM round-trips (D19 start 2.4-2.8 s + download 2.7-3.2 s + submit 1.9 s;\n  solve ~1 s). Parse in memory, never shell out/extract to disk in-window; decompress each member once, cache by\n  (set zip, member).\n- Normalizing a stored value (D13): don't strip braces/reshape a stored string because answer_format sounds generic.\n- Hex width (D10): `\"0x%x\"` drops leading zeros; print `0x%0{2*size}x`. `_rva` = raw field, never ImageBase + it.\n  Require `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew before any PE field; require `\\x7fELF` before any ELF field.\n- Harness: `hctf start` on a solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` (D2) -- restore from `log.jsonl`.\n- Tools installed: exiftool, poppler, qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck, zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost,\n  mediainfo, sqlite3, ImageMagick, readelf/objdump, olevba/oleid, olefile, pefile, pyelftools, LnkParse3, dnfile,\n  mutagen (.venv); msitools under tools/msitools; ffmpeg 7.0.2 (no ffprobe) at\n  `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2` (not on PATH). NOT installed: ffprobe, sox.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UnFm7PMw9YVG9ECVwpFSJQ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a884a1e-870c-4737-be83-7e1c4a09a9ca","uuid":"da067ebd-c748-4639-818f-4bfdd5aa59bd","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:07:19.128Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md","content":"# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-19; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- Every day = ONE evidence zip (plain Deflate, no password so far). D1-7: one tiny member, ONE structural fact. D8-9:\n  the cumulative kit, every field in every mode. D10-14: one member + one field everywhere. **D15+ split the modes**:\n  single = 1 field (the new member), TT = cumulative kit (D15 20 -> D19 24 fields, +1 per day = the day's new member),\n  Mastery = 5 kits x the TT set, incl. a cross-member \"synthesis\" question every day. Pre-arm EVERY earlier family AND\n  the synthesis before the timed run; the timed field set is not the single's.\n- Member families: note/text -> jpg -> png -> pdf -> inner zip -> Go PE (D9-11) -> .NET dll (D12) -> MSI (D13) -> LNK\n  (D14) -> OOXML `.docx` (D15) -> `.eml` (D16) -> RIFF/WAVE audio (D17) -> MP4 h264+aac video (D18) -> Linux ELF (D19).\n  The fmt word is sometimes an ABSTRACT namespace (`email` not `eml`; `media` for BOTH audio D17 and video D18, with\n  ffprobe vocabulary) and sometimes the plain format (`elf` D19, like `pe`/`msi`/`lnk`) -- read it, never guess it.\n- A new `<fmt>.<field>` each day: identity -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` -> `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` ->\n  `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries` -> `zip.central_directory_member_names`\n  -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` -> `pe.version_original_filename` ->\n  `dotnet.mvid_guid` -> `msi.product_code_guid` -> `lnk.target_path_windows` -> `ooxml.external_relationship_targets` ->\n  `email.message_id` -> `media.primary_audio_codec_name` -> `media.primary_video_dimensions` -> `elf.e_machine_u16_hex`.\n  The question names the field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); ids `dNN-<family>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_`\n  -> `-`); `dNN` = the family's first day; `<family>` != `<fmt>` for media (`d17-audio-001-media-`, `d18-video-...`).\n- The flavor text promises extra findings (\"the collision\", \"the impossible destination\", \"equivalent recordings\",\n  \"crops ... the claimed device\", D19 \"Linux binaries from several systems ... rebuild deployment groups\") that were\n  NEVER asked; the sample usually delivers less (D9 \"several architectures\" -> one i386 PE; D19 \"several systems\" -> one\n  x86-64 ELF). The graded field is the STRUCTURAL truth from header bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the\n  lie. Pre-arm siblings without guessing spellings. Titles are puns (D19 \"Little Endian\" = ELF EI_DATA byte order).\n- Singles: D1-9 first-submit CORRECT ~27-60 s; D10, D13, D15 lost ONE submit to a convention (padding, braces, list\n  order); D16 lost TWO (parser -> `none`, stripped brackets); D17 ~24 s; D18 ~5 s and D19 ~13 s (race probe answered\n  from the prebuilt `lib.meta` registry before any LLM work). TT/Mastery: CORRECT every day, but D15-D17 AND D19 only\n  after an offline generalize (synthesis dispatch missing from the day's solver); D18 in-window first try.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\". Container NAMES drift: D1-14 `metadata-day-NN-evidence[-0N].zip`;\n  D15-19 TT `evidence.zip`, Mastery `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..05.zip`. Route by the ref's text before\n  `->` and by sha256, never a hard-coded name.\n- **Field-set size** -- per mode: D7 TT 11 / Mastery 22; D8-9 12-13 everywhere; D10-14 one; D15 1/20/100; D16 1/21/105;\n  D17 1/22/110; D18 1/23/115; D19 1/24/120. Families: identity + `d04-jpeg-*`, `d05-png-*`, `d06-pdf-*`, `d07-zip-*`\n  (eocd + CD names), `d09-pe-*` (machine, entry RVA, OriginalFilename), `d12-dotnet-*`, `d13-msi-*`, `d14-lnk-*`,\n  `d15-ooxml-*`, `d16-email-*`, `d17-audio-*`, `d18-video-*`, `d19-elf-*` + synthesis. Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX\n  (reference solver answering all 24: `challenges/day19/metadata-little-endian-on-the-prairie/solver/solve.py`).\n- **fmt word vs registry key vs id family word** (D16-D19) -- D16 `email.*` (prebuilt said `eml`); D17\n  `media.primary_audio_codec_name` id `d17-audio-...`; D18 `media.primary_video_dimensions` id `d18-video-...` (one\n  `media` namespace spans two families); D19 plain `elf.e_machine_u16_hex` id `d19-elf-001-elf-e-machine-u16-hex`\n  (family = fmt; spec name `e_machine` keeps its own underscore -> `e-machine`). Vocabulary = the field's home tool\n  (ffprobe for media) or the spec struct (`e_machine`, `coff_machine`). Rule: take `<fmt>.<field>` from the QUESTION\n  text (or the slug after `-NNN-`), map fmt synonyms (`email`<->`eml`/`mime`; `media`<->`audio`/`video`/`av`/...),\n  route the extractor by the member's MAGIC, fall back to the same field under any fmt.\n- **Identity member roster** (D15+) -- THREE small text members (`evidence-note.txt` 33 B, `evidence-note-copy.txt`\n  33 B, `roster.csv` 29 B); EACH identity question picks one at random per set: ids `<member-stem>-{filename,size-bytes,\n  md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}`. The filename question's artifact = the container only\n  (\"the exact filename of the roster\") -> map the id stem to the member. Never assume `evidence-note-*`.\n- **Synthesis / cross-member** (D15+) -- id `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<algo>-order` (TODAY's NN), kind `json`, norm\n  `case_insensitive`: \"Compute the full-file SHA-256 digest of each named file, then submit a compact JSON array of\n  their filenames in ascending digest order. Files: [...]\". The `artifact` names ONE member; the inputs are the\n  `Files:` list, same container. Rule: regex `Files:\\s*(\\[.*?\\])`, resolve each under the ref's container,\n  `hashlib.new(algo)` over raw bytes, sort by hex digest (descending only if said), emit names --\n  `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo)`, get_bytes bound to the artifacts root INSIDE the per-set\n  worker. Shape: note + 2 re-picked kit members (jpg/exe/docx D15, png/dll D17, png/msi D18, pdf/lnk D19) + TODAY's\n  member; order re-rolls per set. Only sha256 seen so far -- expect md5/sha1/size/time/arch-group siblings.\n- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree with the\n  header: answer from the structural bytes of the member the question names. D19 kit pools `collector-001.elf` with\n  `MZ` members (`telemetry-agent-001.exe`, `managed-001.dll`): an `elf.*` field of a non-ELF = literal `none`.\n- **Member values** -- re-roll per variant; never cache across sets. Seen re-rolled: note case id; D7 entry count\n  2-5; jpg/png dims per set (423x1089, 1255x1059); D10 entry RVA; D11 PE arch (0x014c/0x8664/0xaa64, OriginalFilename\n  `pe-base-<goarch>.exe` follows); D12 MVID; synthesis order. Constant so far (don't rely on it): D13 ProductCode,\n  D14 lnk target, D15 docx targets, kit exe/dll/msi/lnk, D17 codec `pcm_s16le`, D18 video `320x180`, D19 ELF (the same\n  14 408-B x86-64 LSB ELF64 ET_EXEC in single, TT and all 5 Mastery sets) -- the flavors' transcodes/crops/\"several\n  systems\" (big-endian MIPS/PPC, ARM, i386) are still due: read every ELF field with the file's own EI_CLASS/EI_DATA.\n- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes case-insensitive; `0x`-hex is `trim` only -> lowercase),\n  `enum` (`accepted_values`), `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact values and order\"). Emit per kind; read\n  `syntax` for prefix/case. JSON ORDER is field-specific -- see conventions.\n- **Question-text tags** -- D9 timed: ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<64 hex>]` suffix; D15+ timed: ``Inspect `<member>`. ``\n  prefix. Strip both before reading names; route by id + `artifact`.\n- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer\n  from an enclosing zip. An OOXML member is itself a zip -- parse it as the asked member, not as a wrapper to descend.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | python `zipfile` read of the member in memory (`7z l -slt` for orientation) |\n| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the member bytes; the id stem names WHICH member |\n| \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |\n| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`) -> `true`/`false` |\n| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width |\n| `png.ihdr_*` | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n| `zip.eocd_*` | of the NAMED zip: last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+10 total entries, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 (`PK\\x06\\x07` -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32) |\n| `zip.central_directory_*` | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from cd offset: name len @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name @+46. Raw stored path, CD order, no dedupe/sort; UTF-8 if flag 0x800 else UTF-8-then-cp437 |\n| `pdf.header_version` | `head -c 16 f | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; catalog `/Version` is a diagnostic only |\n| `pe.coff_*` | `MZ` -> e_lfanew u32 @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` -> Machine u16 @+4; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b`/`0x20b`) |\n| `pe.address_of_entry_point_*` / `pe.image_base*` | opt = e_lfanew+24: AddressOfEntryPoint u32 @opt+16 (RVA); ImageBase @opt+28 (PE32) / u64 @opt+24 (PE32+). objdump \"start address\" is the VA |\n| `pe.version_*` | `pefile` resource dir only -> `FileInfo..StringTable..entries`; id tail -> key ignoring case/`-_`. Shell: `strings -e l f.exe \\| grep -A1 OriginalFilename` |\n| `elf.*` (`7f 45 4c 46`) | EI_CLASS @4 (1=32, 2=64), EI_DATA @5 (1=LSB `<`, 2=MSB `>`) picks the struct byte order for EVERYTHING after @16: e_type u16 @16, e_machine u16 @18, e_version u32 @20, e_entry @24 (u32/u64 by class). `xxd -s 16 -l 4 f` + `readelf -h f`. In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `elf` (~45 fields: ei_*, e_type, e_entry_hex, e_flags, interp, build-id, section names). D19 `3e 00` LSB -> `0x003e` |\n| `macho.*` (promised, not yet asked) | `feedface`/`feedfacf` (BE) or `cefaedfe`/`cffaedfe` (LE) cputype u32 @4; fat `cafebabe` BE nfat_arch @4 (Java class shares the magic: major version @6 >= 45). `lib.meta` fmt `macho` |\n| `dotnet.*` / Mono assembly | data dir 14 -> CLI header -> `BSJB` -> `#~` (HeapSizes @+6, Valid @+8, rows @+24) -> Module row 0 Mvid (1-based #GUID idx) -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..)`. `lib/meta/dotnet.py` |\n| `msi.*` / `.msi` (OLE `d0 cf 11 e0`) | fast: `strings -n 6 x.msi \\| grep -aoE 'ProductCode\\{[0-9A-F-]{36}\\}'`; exact: CFB streams -> `!_StringPool`/`!_StringData` -> `!Property` (column-major). `olefile` in venv; `day13/.../solve.py msi_property` |\n| `lnk.*` / `.lnk` (`4c 00 00 00` + CLSID 00021401) | LinkFlags @0x14 (0x1 IDList, 0x2 LinkInfo, 0x80 Unicode); target = LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+CommonPathSuffix) verbatim, else IDList. `lib.meta.lnk:target_path` |\n| `ooxml.*` / `.docx/.xlsx/.pptx` (`PK` + `[Content_Types].xml`) | zip of XML parts. Relationships live in EVERY `*.rels` part. External = `TargetMode=\"External\"` (case-insensitive; absent = Internal). `unzip -p f.docx '*.rels' \\| grep -o 'Target=\"[^\"]*\" TargetMode=\"External\"'`; solver: `zipfile` + ElementTree over every `.rels`, local-name `Relationship` |\n| `email.*` / `.eml` (text `From:`/`Message-ID:`/`MIME-Version:`, CRLF) | `grep -ai '^message-id' f.eml`; solver: `lib.meta.prebuilt.eml.eml_value(data, {\"field\": f})` (stdlib `email`, unfolded raw header). Values VERBATIM (Message-ID keeps `<...>`). Threading = `In-Reply-To`/`References`/`Message-ID` |\n| `media.*` / audio (`RIFF..WAVE`, `ID3`/`ff fb`, `OggS`, `fLaC`, `ftyp`, `1a 45 df a3`, `FORM..AIFF`, `#!AMR`) | route by MAGIC. WAV: RIFF chunks from @12 to `fmt ` -> wFormatTag u16 @+8, bits u16 @+22 (0xFFFE -> SubFormat GUID first u16 @+32) -> FFmpeg names (Conventions). Truth: `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2 -hide_banner -i f` (no ffprobe; `mediainfo` says `PCM` = wrong vocabulary). In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `media`/`audio`/`av` |\n| `media.*video*` / MP4-MOV (`....ftyp`), MKV/WebM, AVI | box walk `moov` -> first `trak` whose `mdia/hdlr` = `vide` -> `stsd` entry: w,h u16 BE @entry+32; cross-check tkhd w/h + matrix, `pasp`, `clap`, SPS crop (may DISAGREE in a variant). In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `media`/`video` (`prebuilt/media_video.py`). Truth: bundled `ffmpeg -i` -> `Video: h264 (High) ..., 320x180 [SAR 1:1 DAR 16:9]` |\n| `*-synthesis-<algo>-order` / \"Files: [...]\" in the question | parse the list from the question text, hash each member of the same container, sort by digest, compact JSON of names |\n| GUID field (`*-guid`) | spelling follows the SOURCE: stored string (MSI) verbatim braces+uppercase; binary (.NET) -> lowercase, no braces |\n| exe-extension decoy (`MZ` without `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit |\n| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\", \"pooled with ... renamed data\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)`; decide ORDER per field (conventions) |\n| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids | resolve each set's container separately; see delivery layouts |\n\n## Day by day\n**Days 1-14** (one field each, all timed first try): D1 identity -> D2 `magic-prefix-hex-16` -> D3 BOM -> D4 JPEG SOFn\n`<w>x<h>` -> D5 PNG IHDR -> D6 `pdf.header_version` `x.y` -> D7 `zip.eocd_total_entries` of the INNER zip -> D8 CD names\n(compact JSON, CD order) -> D9-11 one Go PE: `coff_machine_u16_hex` `0x014c`, entry RVA `0x%08x` (unpadded REJECTED),\n`version_original_filename` verbatim -> D12 `dotnet.mvid_guid` (`uuid.UUID(bytes_le)` lowercase, no braces) -> D13\n`msi.product_code_guid` (stored WITH braces; brace-less REJECTED) -> D14 `lnk.target_path_windows` (LinkInfo path).\n\n**Days 15-18** (single = 1 new-family field; TT/Mastery = cumulative kit + synthesis): D15 \"A Word to the Wise\"\n`ooxml.external_relationship_targets` (`.docx` rels `TargetMode=\"External\"` -> Targets SORTED; rels order REJECTED,\n+50 s). D16 \"Return to Sender\" `email.message_id` (VERBATIM with `<>`; lost 2 submits: id regex hit the first `email-`\n-> `none`, then stripped brackets). D17 \"Hear Me Out\" `media.primary_audio_codec_name` (RIFF PCM 16-bit mono -> ffprobe\nname `pcm_s16le`, not `PCM`/`0x0001`; ~24 s). D18 \"Frame of Reference\" `media.primary_video_dimensions` (`video-001.mp4`\nh264 High + aac; first `vide` trak's stsd w x h = `320x180`, lowercase `x`; the audio trak must not be picked; race\nprobe answered from prebuilt `media_video.py` in ~5 s). D15-D17 timed: `synthesis-sha256-order` missing from the day's\ntemplate -> `solver_incomplete` -> offline generalize -> CORRECT. D18: the single worker pre-wired the synthesis ->\nTT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try.\n\n**Day 19 — Little Endian on the Prairie** (`elf.e_machine_u16_hex`, kind `pattern` \"lowercase hexadecimal with a 0x\nprefix and no explanatory text\", norm `trim`, id `d19-elf-001-elf-e-machine-u16-hex`). Prompt: \"Linux binaries from\nseveral systems have been pooled with Windows executables and renamed data. Determine architecture directly from the\nELF header and rebuild deployment groups.\" (several systems / renamed data / deployment groups -- NOT asked).\n- Artifact: 1 849-B zip -> `collector-001.elf` (14 408 B): ELF64 (EI_CLASS 2) LSB (EI_DATA 1), OSABI 0 SYSV, ET_EXEC\n  (2), x86-64, dynamically linked, PT_INTERP `/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2`, `.note.ABI-tag` GNU/Linux 3.2.0, stripped,\n  no `.note.gnu.build-id`. Bytes @18 = `3e 00`.\n- Key insight: the title pun IS the field rule -- read e_machine with the byte order EI_DATA declares (`<H` here, `>H`\n  for MSB MIPS/PPC/s390x/SPARC), then spell it like D9's `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`: `0x` + 4 lowercase zero-padded\n  digits = `0x003e` (not `0x3e`, not `x86-64`/`EM_X86_64`/`62`). Common values: i386 `0x0003`, SPARC `0x0002`, MIPS\n  `0x0008`, PPC `0x0014`, PPC64 `0x0015`, s390 `0x0016`, ARM `0x0028`, SPARCV9 `0x002b`, x86-64 `0x003e`, AArch64\n  `0x00b7`, RISC-V `0x00f3`, LoongArch `0x0102`.\n- Tools: none by hand -- the race probe answered from `lib.meta` fmt `elf` (D18-night `elf-header` prebuild; tier still\n  `speculative`; a synthesized MSB MIPS header answers `0x0008`, a PE/text member `none`). Manual: `xxd -s 4 -l 2 f`\n  (class, data) + `xxd -s 18 -l 2 f`; `readelf -h f` \"Machine: Advanced Micro Devices X86-64\".\n- Single CORRECT on the first submit ~13 s after start (race transport 3.1 s). The single worker then added an explicit\n  endian-aware extractor to `solve.py` but NOT the synthesis dispatch -> TT (24 fields; 23 verified in-window 6.0 s)\n  and Mastery (120; 115 verified in-window 6.0 s) both `solver_incomplete` on `metadata-day-19-synthesis-sha256-order`\n  (Files: note + `document-001.pdf` + `shortcut-001.lnk` + `collector-001.elf`) -> generalize ported D18's\n  `synthesis-<algo>-order` branch (+ `_ROOT` set inside `_solve_pairs`) -> TT CORRECT (2 generalize workers),\n  Mastery CORRECT (1). Same failure as D15-D17: the regression was the template, not the parse.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`). Booleans: enum `true` / `false`.\n- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR, video `media.primary_video_dimensions` D18): `<width>x<height>`, lowercase\n  `x`, no spaces. Video = ffprobe width/height of v:0 (coded size, NOT rotated, not the tkhd display size).\n- PDF header version: bare `x.y`; absent -> literal `none` (wording; `none` not yet GM-confirmed). Counts: plain integer.\n- JSON lists -- compact, double quotes, no spaces; ORDER depends on the field:\n  - `zip.central_directory_member_names`: full stored paths in CD order (`[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]`).\n  - `ooxml.external_relationship_targets`: Target strings SORTED ascending (D15 all modes); rels-file order REJECTED.\n  - `*-synthesis-<algo>-order`: member names ordered by hex digest ascending (D15-D19 TT/Mastery; `case_insensitive`).\n  Heuristic: a list read off one on-disk structure that the field name calls \"names in the directory\" keeps disk\n  order; a set gathered across parts (\"targets\", \"dependencies\") is sorted. If an order is rejected, try the other.\n- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 PE Machine\n  `0x014c`, u16 ELF e_machine `0x003e` (D19), u32 AddressOfEntryPoint `0x00065bd0`. Width from the STRUCT / the\n  `_uNN_` in the id; the value from the file's own byte order (ELF EI_DATA). (Magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; the\n  binary lane's machine wants `i386` and accepted unpadded entry points -- different generator.)\n- GUIDs: .NET MVID `Guid.ToString()` lowercase no braces (D12); MSI ProductCode the stored string uppercase WITH braces\n  (D13). Spelling follows the source, not answer_format.\n- Windows paths (`lnk.target_path_windows`): stored LinkInfo path verbatim (backslashes, case, drive letter, no quotes).\n- Version-resource strings (`pe.version_<field>`): StringFileInfo value verbatim incl. extension.\n- URLs (`ooxml` Targets): the attribute value verbatim -- scheme, host, path as stored; no trailing-slash or case fixups.\n- E-mail headers (`email.<field>`): header value as stored after RFC 5322 unfolding; Message-ID WITH `<>` (D16).\n- Media codec names (`media.*codec_name`, D17): FFmpeg/ffprobe `codec_name`, lowercase: WAV tag 1 -> `pcm_u8` (8-bit) /\n  `pcm_s16le` / `pcm_s24le` / `pcm_s32le` (RIFX -> `..be`); tag 3 -> `pcm_f32le`/`pcm_f64le`; 6 `pcm_alaw`; 7\n  `pcm_mulaw`; 2 `adpcm_ms`; 0x11 `adpcm_ima_wav`; 0x55 `mp3`; 0xFFFE -> SubFormat GUID first u16. Others: `mp3`, `aac`,\n  `opus`, `vorbis`, `flac`, `alac`, `amr_nb`/`amr_wb`, `ac3`. Only `pcm_s16le` is GM-verified.\n- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` (D10, unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-file-order target list (D15);\n  bracket-less Message-ID (D16). Pattern: delimiters that are part of the stored value (`{}`, `<>`) stay.\n- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_` = SOF header, `eocd_total_entries` = the EOCD's own claim,\n  `e_machine` = Elf_Ehdr member) -- read it literally to pick the structure. A claimed count is NOT a CD walk; CD\n  names are NOT local-header names; `_uNN_hex` fixes read+print width. Unverified ELF siblings: bare enum-ish fields\n  (`ei_data`, `e_type`) have no GM spelling yet -- lib emits `ELFDATA2LSB` / `2`; prefer the `_hex` form if offered.\n\n## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (filename questions: artifact = the zip only).\n- Mastery zip-of-zips (days 1,2,4,5,7,8,10,11,14,15-19): ONE download (`...-evidence-01.zip`; D15+ `evidence-01.zip`)\n  holding `-01.zip`..`-0N.zip`, each holding its set's member(s) (D7 three levels; D8/D15+ five full kits). Refs\n  `<set zip> -> <member>`; every set reuses member names -> resolve by (set zip, member).\n- Mastery day 9: download named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip` while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip` ->\n  resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not its filename.\n- Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` refs.\n- Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) -- never hardcode names.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Synthesis dispatch lost AGAIN (D15, D16, D17, D19)**: every day the single's `solve.py` answers the new field but the\n  timed kit adds `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-sha256-order` -> `solver_incomplete` -> an offline generalize (~1 min per\n  mode). D18 was clean only because the single worker pre-wired it. Right after single CORRECT: `grep -n synthesis\n  solver/solve.py` must show a dispatch calling `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order`, with the artifacts root set INSIDE\n  the per-set worker (`_solve_pairs`; Mastery forks one process per set), plus identity for ANY member stem and every\n  carry-over family. Start from the previous day's solver, not a fresh template.\n- Id-slug parsing (D16, 1 wrong): ids repeat the fmt word (`d16-email-001-email-message-id`); a regex on the first\n  `email-` yields `001-email-message-id` -> lookup miss -> `none`. Anchor `-\\d+-<fmt>-(.+)$`. Never submit `none`\n  without grepping the bytes for the field -- `none` means absent in the artifact, not \"my parser returned None\".\n- Registry misses (D14 key one suffix short `lnk.target_path`; D16 fmt `eml` vs GM `email`; D17 `wav.*` vs `media.*`):\n  `python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print([k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'])\"` and grep\n  `lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` for the FIELD name; call the nearest extractor directly before writing one. D18 (`media`)\n  and D19 (`elf`) both HIT the prebuilt registry -> answered in the race probe.\n- Endianness (D19 pun): never `struct.unpack('<H')` an ELF/Mach-O field blindly -- EI_DATA (ELF @5) / the Mach-O magic\n  byte order decide; ELF32 vs ELF64 moves every offset after e_version (e_entry/e_phoff/e_shoff widths).\n- Video geometry has FOUR sources (D18 they agreed; \"crops / impossible device\" flavor says variants won't): stsd\n  sample-entry w/h, codec SPS (h264 frame_cropping -> ffprobe `width`/`height`), tkhd 16.16 display w/h, tkhd matrix\n  rotation (ffprobe keeps coded dims). If a variant's stsd and SPS disagree, trust the SPS-cropped size, note it.\n- Field suffix picks the spelling: `_u16_hex` = the raw struct value (D9: not `i386`/GOARCH; D19: not `x86-64`);\n  `_codec_name` = the tool vocabulary (D17: `pcm_s16le`, not the raw format tag `1` nor mediainfo's `PCM`).\n- JSON list ORDER (D15, 1 wrong + ~26 s): \"exact values and order\" does not say WHICH order. File order was rejected\n  for rels targets; sorted won. Decide per field (conventions above) before the first submit.\n- Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (D2 TT); a pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the 409\n  `start_required` body (questions, NO `answer_ids`). Answer under the live `answer_ids`.\n- Don't let the flavor text widen the question: only the named field is graded; extra checks are diagnostics.\n- Container-of-containers: a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded zip reads the OUTER EOCD, a name lookup on\n  zip-of-zips returned `PK` as the \"magic\". Resolve the named member's bytes first (recurse), then parse.\n- Name-list fields: emit CD bytes as-is for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `\\`, dupes). Decoy names (`*-with-bom.txt`,\n  `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF): bytes win every time.\n- Timed windows are seconds; most of it is GM round-trips (D19 start 2.4-2.8 s + download 2.7-3.2 s + submit 1.9 s;\n  solve ~1 s). Parse in memory, never shell out/extract to disk in-window; decompress each member once, cache by\n  (set zip, member).\n- Normalizing a stored value (D13): don't strip braces/reshape a stored string because answer_format sounds generic.\n- Hex width (D10): `\"0x%x\"` drops leading zeros; print `0x%0{2*size}x`. `_rva` = raw field, never ImageBase + it.\n  Require `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew before any PE field; require `\\x7fELF` before any ELF field.\n- Harness: `hctf start` on a solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` (D2) -- restore from `log.jsonl`.\n- Tools installed: exiftool, poppler, qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck, zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost,\n  mediainfo, sqlite3, ImageMagick, readelf/objdump, olevba/oleid, olefile, pefile, pyelftools, LnkParse3, dnfile,\n  mutagen (.venv); msitools under tools/msitools; ffmpeg 7.0.2 (no ffprobe) at\n  `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2` (not on PATH). NOT installed: ffprobe, sox.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":48,"newStart":1,"newLines":50,"lines":["-# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-18; updated after every day)","+# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-19; updated after every day)"," "," How this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):"," - **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a","   guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field."," - Every day = ONE evidence zip (plain Deflate, no password so far). D1-7: one tiny member, ONE structural fact. D8-9:","   the cumulative kit, every field in every mode. D10-14: one member + one field everywhere. **D15+ split the modes**:","-  single = 1 field (the new member), TT = cumulative kit (D15 20 -> D18 23 fields, +1 per day = the day's new member),","+  single = 1 field (the new member), TT = cumulative kit (D15 20 -> D19 24 fields, +1 per day = the day's new member),","   Mastery = 5 kits x the TT set, incl. a cross-member \"synthesis\" question every day. Pre-arm EVERY earlier family AND","   the synthesis before the timed run; the timed field set is not the single's."," - Member families: note/text -> jpg -> png -> pdf -> inner zip -> Go PE (D9-11) -> .NET dll (D12) -> MSI (D13) -> LNK","-  (D14) -> OOXML `.docx` (D15) -> `.eml` (D16) -> RIFF/WAVE audio (D17) -> MP4 h264+aac video (D18). The fmt word is","-  the GM's ABSTRACT namespace, not the container: `email` (not `eml`), `media` for BOTH audio (D17) and video (D18) --","-  and media fields use ffprobe's vocabulary.","+  (D14) -> OOXML `.docx` (D15) -> `.eml` (D16) -> RIFF/WAVE audio (D17) -> MP4 h264+aac video (D18) -> Linux ELF (D19).","+  The fmt word is sometimes an ABSTRACT namespace (`email` not `eml`; `media` for BOTH audio D17 and video D18, with","+  ffprobe vocabulary) and sometimes the plain format (`elf` D19, like `pe`/`msi`/`lnk`) -- read it, never guess it."," - A new `<fmt>.<field>` each day: identity -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` -> `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` ->","   `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries` -> `zip.central_directory_member_names`","   -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` -> `pe.version_original_filename` ->","   `dotnet.mvid_guid` -> `msi.product_code_guid` -> `lnk.target_path_windows` -> `ooxml.external_relationship_targets` ->","-  `email.message_id` -> `media.primary_audio_codec_name` -> `media.primary_video_dimensions`. The question names the","-  field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); ids `dNN-<family>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`); `dNN` = the","-  family's first day; `<family>` != `<fmt>` for media (`d17-audio-001-media-`, `d18-video-001-media-`).","+  `email.message_id` -> `media.primary_audio_codec_name` -> `media.primary_video_dimensions` -> `elf.e_machine_u16_hex`.","+  The question names the field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); ids `dNN-<family>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_`","+  -> `-`); `dNN` = the family's first day; `<family>` != `<fmt>` for media (`d17-audio-001-media-`, `d18-video-...`)."," - The flavor text promises extra findings (\"the collision\", \"the impossible destination\", \"equivalent recordings\",","-  \"crops, the recording that could not have come from the claimed device\") that were NEVER asked; the sample usually","-  delivers less (D9 \"several architectures\" -> one i386 PE). The graded field is the STRUCTURAL truth from header bytes;","-  names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. Pre-arm siblings without guessing spellings. Titles are puns.","+  \"crops ... the claimed device\", D19 \"Linux binaries from several systems ... rebuild deployment groups\") that were","+  NEVER asked; the sample usually delivers less (D9 \"several architectures\" -> one i386 PE; D19 \"several systems\" -> one","+  x86-64 ELF). The graded field is the STRUCTURAL truth from header bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the","+  lie. Pre-arm siblings without guessing spellings. Titles are puns (D19 \"Little Endian\" = ELF EI_DATA byte order)."," - Singles: D1-9 first-submit CORRECT ~27-60 s; D10, D13, D15 lost ONE submit to a convention (padding, braces, list","-  order); D16 lost TWO (parser -> `none`, stripped brackets); D17 ~24 s; D18 ~5 s (race probe answered from the prebuilt","-  `lib.meta` registry before any LLM work). TT/Mastery: first GM submit CORRECT since D4, but D15-D17 only after an","-  offline generalize (synthesis missing); D18 in-window first try (single worker pre-wired the synthesis).","+  order); D16 lost TWO (parser -> `none`, stripped brackets); D17 ~24 s; D18 ~5 s and D19 ~13 s (race probe answered","+  from the prebuilt `lib.meta` registry before any LLM work). TT/Mastery: CORRECT every day, but D15-D17 AND D19 only","+  after an offline generalize (synthesis dispatch missing from the day's solver); D18 in-window first try."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)"," - **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\". Container NAMES drift: D1-14 `metadata-day-NN-evidence[-0N].zip`;","-  D15-18 TT `evidence.zip`, Mastery `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..05.zip`. Route by the ref's text before","+  D15-19 TT `evidence.zip`, Mastery `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..05.zip`. Route by the ref's text before","   `->` and by sha256, never a hard-coded name."," - **Field-set size** -- per mode: D7 TT 11 / Mastery 22; D8-9 12-13 everywhere; D10-14 one; D15 1/20/100; D16 1/21/105;","-  D17 1/22/110; D18 1/23/115. Families: identity + `d04-jpeg-*`, `d05-png-*`, `d06-pdf-*`, `d07-zip-*` (eocd + CD","-  names), `d09-pe-*` (machine, entry RVA, OriginalFilename), `d12-dotnet-*`, `d13-msi-*`, `d14-lnk-*`, `d15-ooxml-*`,","-  `d16-email-*`, `d17-audio-*`, `d18-video-*` + synthesis. Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX (reference solver answering","-  all 23: `challenges/day18/metadata-frame-of-reference/solver/solve.py`).","-- **fmt word vs registry key vs id family word** (D16-D18) -- D16 `email.*` (prebuilt said `eml`); D17","+  D17 1/22/110; D18 1/23/115; D19 1/24/120. Families: identity + `d04-jpeg-*`, `d05-png-*`, `d06-pdf-*`, `d07-zip-*`","+  (eocd + CD names), `d09-pe-*` (machine, entry RVA, OriginalFilename), `d12-dotnet-*`, `d13-msi-*`, `d14-lnk-*`,","+  `d15-ooxml-*`, `d16-email-*`, `d17-audio-*`, `d18-video-*`, `d19-elf-*` + synthesis. Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX","+  (reference solver answering all 24: `challenges/day19/metadata-little-endian-on-the-prairie/solver/solve.py`).","+- **fmt word vs registry key vs id family word** (D16-D19) -- D16 `email.*` (prebuilt said `eml`); D17","   `media.primary_audio_codec_name` id `d17-audio-...`; D18 `media.primary_video_dimensions` id `d18-video-...` (one","-  `media` namespace spans two families). Vocabulary = ffprobe (`primary_<type>_` = first stream of that type in","-  container order, `codec_name` = FFmpeg id, `dimensions` = `<width>x<height>`). Rule: take `<fmt>.<field>` from the","-  QUESTION text (or the slug after `-NNN-`), map fmt synonyms (`email`<->`eml`/`mime`; `media`<->`audio`/`video`/`av`/","-  `wav`/`mp4`/...), route the extractor by the member's MAGIC, fall back to the same field under any fmt.","+  `media` namespace spans two families); D19 plain `elf.e_machine_u16_hex` id `d19-elf-001-elf-e-machine-u16-hex`","+  (family = fmt; spec name `e_machine` keeps its own underscore -> `e-machine`). Vocabulary = the field's home tool","+  (ffprobe for media) or the spec struct (`e_machine`, `coff_machine`). Rule: take `<fmt>.<field>` from the QUESTION","+  text (or the slug after `-NNN-`), map fmt synonyms (`email`<->`eml`/`mime`; `media`<->`audio`/`video`/`av`/...),","+  route the extractor by the member's MAGIC, fall back to the same field under any fmt."," - **Identity member roster** (D15+) -- THREE small text members (`evidence-note.txt` 33 B, `evidence-note-copy.txt`","   33 B, `roster.csv` 29 B); EACH identity question picks one at random per set: ids `<member-stem>-{filename,size-bytes,","   md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}`. The filename question's artifact = the container only"]},{"oldStart":53,"oldLines":15,"newStart":55,"newLines":17,"lines":["   `Files:` list, same container. Rule: regex `Files:\\s*(\\[.*?\\])`, resolve each under the ref's container,","   `hashlib.new(algo)` over raw bytes, sort by hex digest (descending only if said), emit names --","   `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo)`, get_bytes bound to the artifacts root INSIDE the per-set","-  worker. Shape: note + 2 re-picked kit members (jpg/exe/docx D15, png/dll D17, png/msi D18) + TODAY's member; order","-  re-rolls per set. Only sha256 seen so far -- expect md5/sha1/size/time siblings.","+  worker. Shape: note + 2 re-picked kit members (jpg/exe/docx D15, png/dll D17, png/msi D18, pdf/lnk D19) + TODAY's","+  member; order re-rolls per set. Only sha256 seen so far -- expect md5/sha1/size/time/arch-group siblings."," - **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree with the","-  header: answer from the structural bytes of the member the question names.","+  header: answer from the structural bytes of the member the question names. D19 kit pools `collector-001.elf` with","+  `MZ` members (`telemetry-agent-001.exe`, `managed-001.dll`): an `elf.*` field of a non-ELF = literal `none`."," - **Member values** -- re-roll per variant; never cache across sets. Seen re-rolled: note case id; D7 entry count","   2-5; jpg/png dims per set (423x1089, 1255x1059); D10 entry RVA; D11 PE arch (0x014c/0x8664/0xaa64, OriginalFilename","   `pe-base-<goarch>.exe` follows); D12 MVID; synthesis order. Constant so far (don't rely on it): D13 ProductCode,","-  D14 lnk target, D15 docx targets, kit exe/dll/msi/lnk, D17 codec `pcm_s16le`, D18 video `320x180` (h264 High 10 fps;","-  stsd = tkhd = SPS, identity matrix, pasp 1:1 in every set) -- the flavor's transcodes/crops/rotations are still due.","+  D14 lnk target, D15 docx targets, kit exe/dll/msi/lnk, D17 codec `pcm_s16le`, D18 video `320x180`, D19 ELF (the same","+  14 408-B x86-64 LSB ELF64 ET_EXEC in single, TT and all 5 Mastery sets) -- the flavors' transcodes/crops/\"several","+  systems\" (big-endian MIPS/PPC, ARM, i386) are still due: read every ELF field with the file's own EI_CLASS/EI_DATA."," - **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes case-insensitive; `0x`-hex is `trim` only -> lowercase),","   `enum` (`accepted_values`), `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact values and order\"). Emit per kind; read","   `syntax` for prefix/case. JSON ORDER is field-specific -- see conventions."]},{"oldStart":85,"oldLines":18,"newStart":89,"newLines":19,"lines":[" | `pe.coff_*` | `MZ` -> e_lfanew u32 @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` -> Machine u16 @+4; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b`/`0x20b`) |"," | `pe.address_of_entry_point_*` / `pe.image_base*` | opt = e_lfanew+24: AddressOfEntryPoint u32 @opt+16 (RVA); ImageBase @opt+28 (PE32) / u64 @opt+24 (PE32+). objdump \"start address\" is the VA |"," | `pe.version_*` | `pefile` resource dir only -> `FileInfo..StringTable..entries`; id tail -> key ignoring case/`-_`. Shell: `strings -e l f.exe \\| grep -A1 OriginalFilename` |","-| `elf.*` / `macho.*` (promised, not yet asked) | ELF `\\x7fELF`, EI_DATA @5, e_machine u16 @18. Mach-O `feedface`/`feedfacf` cputype @4; fat `cafebabe` BE nfat_arch @4 |","+| `elf.*` (`7f 45 4c 46`) | EI_CLASS @4 (1=32, 2=64), EI_DATA @5 (1=LSB `<`, 2=MSB `>`) picks the struct byte order for EVERYTHING after @16: e_type u16 @16, e_machine u16 @18, e_version u32 @20, e_entry @24 (u32/u64 by class). `xxd -s 16 -l 4 f` + `readelf -h f`. In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `elf` (~45 fields: ei_*, e_type, e_entry_hex, e_flags, interp, build-id, section names). D19 `3e 00` LSB -> `0x003e` |","+| `macho.*` (promised, not yet asked) | `feedface`/`feedfacf` (BE) or `cefaedfe`/`cffaedfe` (LE) cputype u32 @4; fat `cafebabe` BE nfat_arch @4 (Java class shares the magic: major version @6 >= 45). `lib.meta` fmt `macho` |"," | `dotnet.*` / Mono assembly | data dir 14 -> CLI header -> `BSJB` -> `#~` (HeapSizes @+6, Valid @+8, rows @+24) -> Module row 0 Mvid (1-based #GUID idx) -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..)`. `lib/meta/dotnet.py` |"," | `msi.*` / `.msi` (OLE `d0 cf 11 e0`) | fast: `strings -n 6 x.msi \\| grep -aoE 'ProductCode\\{[0-9A-F-]{36}\\}'`; exact: CFB streams -> `!_StringPool`/`!_StringData` -> `!Property` (column-major). `olefile` in venv; `day13/.../solve.py msi_property` |"," | `lnk.*` / `.lnk` (`4c 00 00 00` + CLSID 00021401) | LinkFlags @0x14 (0x1 IDList, 0x2 LinkInfo, 0x80 Unicode); target = LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+CommonPathSuffix) verbatim, else IDList. `lib.meta.lnk:target_path` |","-| `ooxml.*` / `.docx/.xlsx/.pptx` (`PK` + `[Content_Types].xml`) | it's a zip of XML parts. Relationships live in EVERY `*.rels` part (`_rels/.rels`, `word/_rels/document.xml.rels`, header/footer/settings rels). External = `TargetMode=\"External\"` (case-insensitive; absent = Internal). `unzip -p f.docx '*.rels' \\| grep -o 'Target=\"[^\"]*\" TargetMode=\"External\"'`; solver: `zipfile` + ElementTree over every `.rels`, local-name `Relationship`. Core props (`docProps/core.xml`) prebuilt in `lib/meta/prebuilt/ooxml.py`; external rels NOT prebuilt as of D15 |","-| `email.*` / `.eml` (text `From:`/`Message-ID:`/`MIME-Version:`, CRLF) | `grep -ai '^message-id' f.eml` to see the stored value; solver: `lib.meta.prebuilt.eml.eml_value(data, {\"field\": f})` (stdlib `email` parser, unfolded raw header). Header values VERBATIM (Message-ID keeps `<...>`). Threading cues (\"replies, forwards, duplicates\") = `In-Reply-To`/`References`/`Message-ID` |","-| `media.*` / audio (`RIFF..WAVE`, `ID3`/`ff fb`, `OggS`, `fLaC`, `ftyp`, `1a 45 df a3`, `FORM..AIFF`, `#!AMR`) | route by MAGIC (names/extensions lie: \"renamed, transcoded\"). WAV: walk RIFF chunks from @12 to `fmt ` -> wFormatTag u16 @+8, bits u16 @+22 (0xFFFE -> SubFormat GUID's first u16 @+32); map to FFmpeg names (Conventions). ground truth = FFmpeg vocabulary: no ffprobe, but `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2 -hide_banner -i f` prints `Stream #0:0: Audio: pcm_s16le ([1][0][0][0] / 0x0001), 16000 Hz, mono, s16` + format tags (worker-side; `mediainfo` says `PCM` = wrong vocabulary). In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `media`/`audio`/`av` (~500 prebuilt fields since D17 night). LIST/INFO `INAM` carried `Huntress audio evidence <12 hex>` (correlation id candidate) |","-| `media.*video*` / MP4-MOV (`....ftyp`), MKV/WebM (`1a 45 df a3`), AVI (`RIFF..AVI `) | box walk `moov` -> `trak` whose `mdia/hdlr` type = `vide` (first one = `primary_video_`) -> `stsd` sample entry: w,h u16 BE @entry+32 (`avc1`/`hvc1`/`vp09`/`av01`); also read tkhd w/h (16.16 @end) + matrix (rotation), `pasp` (SAR), `clap`, avcC SPS crop -- in a variant these may DISAGREE (see Pitfalls). In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `media`/`video`/`av` (`prebuilt/media_video.py`, ~100 video fields). Truth: bundled `ffmpeg -hide_banner -i f` -> `Video: h264 (High) (avc1 / 0x31637661), yuv420p(progressive), 320x180 [SAR 1:1 DAR 16:9], 10 fps` |","+| `ooxml.*` / `.docx/.xlsx/.pptx` (`PK` + `[Content_Types].xml`) | zip of XML parts. Relationships live in EVERY `*.rels` part. External = `TargetMode=\"External\"` (case-insensitive; absent = Internal). `unzip -p f.docx '*.rels' \\| grep -o 'Target=\"[^\"]*\" TargetMode=\"External\"'`; solver: `zipfile` + ElementTree over every `.rels`, local-name `Relationship` |","+| `email.*` / `.eml` (text `From:`/`Message-ID:`/`MIME-Version:`, CRLF) | `grep -ai '^message-id' f.eml`; solver: `lib.meta.prebuilt.eml.eml_value(data, {\"field\": f})` (stdlib `email`, unfolded raw header). Values VERBATIM (Message-ID keeps `<...>`). Threading = `In-Reply-To`/`References`/`Message-ID` |","+| `media.*` / audio (`RIFF..WAVE`, `ID3`/`ff fb`, `OggS`, `fLaC`, `ftyp`, `1a 45 df a3`, `FORM..AIFF`, `#!AMR`) | route by MAGIC. WAV: RIFF chunks from @12 to `fmt ` -> wFormatTag u16 @+8, bits u16 @+22 (0xFFFE -> SubFormat GUID first u16 @+32) -> FFmpeg names (Conventions). Truth: `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2 -hide_banner -i f` (no ffprobe; `mediainfo` says `PCM` = wrong vocabulary). In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `media`/`audio`/`av` |","+| `media.*video*` / MP4-MOV (`....ftyp`), MKV/WebM, AVI | box walk `moov` -> first `trak` whose `mdia/hdlr` = `vide` -> `stsd` entry: w,h u16 BE @entry+32; cross-check tkhd w/h + matrix, `pasp`, `clap`, SPS crop (may DISAGREE in a variant). In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `media`/`video` (`prebuilt/media_video.py`). Truth: bundled `ffmpeg -i` -> `Video: h264 (High) ..., 320x180 [SAR 1:1 DAR 16:9]` |"," | `*-synthesis-<algo>-order` / \"Files: [...]\" in the question | parse the list from the question text, hash each member of the same container, sort by digest, compact JSON of names |"," | GUID field (`*-guid`) | spelling follows the SOURCE: stored string (MSI) verbatim braces+uppercase; binary (.NET) -> lowercase, no braces |"," | exe-extension decoy (`MZ` without `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit |","-| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |","+| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\", \"pooled with ... renamed data\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |"," | answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)`; decide ORDER per field (conventions) |"," | Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids | resolve each set's container separately; see delivery layouts |"," "]},{"oldStart":107,"oldLines":32,"newStart":112,"newLines":37,"lines":[" `version_original_filename` verbatim -> D12 `dotnet.mvid_guid` (`uuid.UUID(bytes_le)` lowercase, no braces) -> D13"," `msi.product_code_guid` (stored WITH braces; brace-less REJECTED) -> D14 `lnk.target_path_windows` (LinkInfo path)."," ","-**Days 15-17** (single = 1 new-family field; TT/Mastery = cumulative kit + synthesis): D15 \"A Word to the Wise\"","+**Days 15-18** (single = 1 new-family field; TT/Mastery = cumulative kit + synthesis): D15 \"A Word to the Wise\""," `ooxml.external_relationship_targets` (`.docx` rels `TargetMode=\"External\"` -> Targets SORTED; rels order REJECTED,","-+50 s). D16 \"Return to Sender\" `email.message_id` (`message-001.eml`; VERBATIM with `<>`; lost 2 submits: id regex hit","-the first `email-` -> `none`, then stripped brackets). D17 \"Hear Me Out\" `media.primary_audio_codec_name` (`audio-001.wav`","-RIFF PCM 16-bit mono 16 kHz + LIST/INFO `INAM` -> ffprobe name `pcm_s16le`, not `PCM`/`0x0001`; ~24 s; flavor","-\"transcoded, renamed, embedded in mail, equivalent recordings\" never asked). All three: `synthesis-sha256-order`","-missing from the day's template -> `solver_incomplete` -> offline generalize -> CORRECT (D17 Mastery also needed the","-artifacts root set inside the per-set worker).","++50 s). D16 \"Return to Sender\" `email.message_id` (VERBATIM with `<>`; lost 2 submits: id regex hit the first `email-`","+-> `none`, then stripped brackets). D17 \"Hear Me Out\" `media.primary_audio_codec_name` (RIFF PCM 16-bit mono -> ffprobe","+name `pcm_s16le`, not `PCM`/`0x0001`; ~24 s). D18 \"Frame of Reference\" `media.primary_video_dimensions` (`video-001.mp4`","+h264 High + aac; first `vide` trak's stsd w x h = `320x180`, lowercase `x`; the audio trak must not be picked; race","+probe answered from prebuilt `media_video.py` in ~5 s). D15-D17 timed: `synthesis-sha256-order` missing from the day's","+template -> `solver_incomplete` -> offline generalize -> CORRECT. D18: the single worker pre-wired the synthesis ->","+TT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try."," ","-**Day 18 — Frame of Reference** (`media.primary_video_dimensions`, kind `exact_text` \"... use the literal none only when","-the requested field is absent\", norm `trim`, id `d18-video-001-media-primary-video-dimensions`). Prompt: \"Clips,","-previews, and screen recordings have been mixed together. Use stream geometry to identify originals, crops, and the","-recording that could not have come from the claimed device.\" (originals/crops/impossible-device flavor -- NOT asked;","-one MP4 only).","-- Artifact: 18.7 KB zip -> `video-001.mp4` (19 775 B, `ftyp isom` minor 512, brands `isomiso2avc1mp41`, Lavf layout","-  `moov` before `mdat`): trak 1 `vide` h264 High `avc1` 320x180 (`avcC`+`pasp` 1:1+`btrt`, 10 fps, 5 frames, encoder","-  `Lavc libx264`), trak 2 `soun` aac LC 44.1 kHz stereo; `udta/meta` mdta `title` = `Huntress MP4 evidence <12 HEX>`.","-  stsd w/h = tkhd 320.0/180.0 = SPS; tkhd matrix identity (rotation 0).","-- Key insight: it's ffprobe `width`x`height` of stream v:0 spelled like D4/D5 (`<w>x<h>`, lowercase `x`). The audio","-  trak in the same file must not be picked; the first `vide` handler wins.","-- Tools: none needed by hand -- the race probe answered from the prebuilt `lib.meta` `media_video.py` (D17-night","-  `media-video-streams` gap). Manual check: box walk to `stsd` (entry+32) or the bundled ffmpeg `-i` line above.","-- Single CORRECT on the first submit ~5 s after start (submit RTT 1.2 s). The single worker then PRE-WIRED the","-  `synthesis-<algo>-order` dispatch (+ artifacts-root global set in `_solve_pairs`) before the timed runs -> TT 23","-  (in-window 3.5 s) and Mastery 5x23 = 115 (in-window 6.8 s) CORRECT first try, no generalize -- first clean timed day","-  since D14.","+**Day 19 — Little Endian on the Prairie** (`elf.e_machine_u16_hex`, kind `pattern` \"lowercase hexadecimal with a 0x","+prefix and no explanatory text\", norm `trim`, id `d19-elf-001-elf-e-machine-u16-hex`). Prompt: \"Linux binaries from","+several systems have been pooled with Windows executables and renamed data. Determine architecture directly from the","+ELF header and rebuild deployment groups.\" (several systems / renamed data / deployment groups -- NOT asked).","+- Artifact: 1 849-B zip -> `collector-001.elf` (14 408 B): ELF64 (EI_CLASS 2) LSB (EI_DATA 1), OSABI 0 SYSV, ET_EXEC","+  (2), x86-64, dynamically linked, PT_INTERP `/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2`, `.note.ABI-tag` GNU/Linux 3.2.0, stripped,","+  no `.note.gnu.build-id`. Bytes @18 = `3e 00`.","+- Key insight: the title pun IS the field rule -- read e_machine with the byte order EI_DATA declares (`<H` here, `>H`","+  for MSB MIPS/PPC/s390x/SPARC), then spell it like D9's `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`: `0x` + 4 lowercase zero-padded","+  digits = `0x003e` (not `0x3e`, not `x86-64`/`EM_X86_64`/`62`). Common values: i386 `0x0003`, SPARC `0x0002`, MIPS","+  `0x0008`, PPC `0x0014`, PPC64 `0x0015`, s390 `0x0016`, ARM `0x0028`, SPARCV9 `0x002b`, x86-64 `0x003e`, AArch64","+  `0x00b7`, RISC-V `0x00f3`, LoongArch `0x0102`.","+- Tools: none by hand -- the race probe answered from `lib.meta` fmt `elf` (D18-night `elf-header` prebuild; tier still","+  `speculative`; a synthesized MSB MIPS header answers `0x0008`, a PE/text member `none`). Manual: `xxd -s 4 -l 2 f`","+  (class, data) + `xxd -s 18 -l 2 f`; `readelf -h f` \"Machine: Advanced Micro Devices X86-64\".","+- Single CORRECT on the first submit ~13 s after start (race transport 3.1 s). The single worker then added an explicit","+  endian-aware extractor to `solve.py` but NOT the synthesis dispatch -> TT (24 fields; 23 verified in-window 6.0 s)","+  and Mastery (120; 115 verified in-window 6.0 s) both `solver_incomplete` on `metadata-day-19-synthesis-sha256-order`","+  (Files: note + `document-001.pdf` + `shortcut-001.lnk` + `collector-001.elf`) -> generalize ported D18's","+  `synthesis-<algo>-order` branch (+ `_ROOT` set inside `_solve_pairs`) -> TT CORRECT (2 generalize workers),","+  Mastery CORRECT (1). Same failure as D15-D17: the regression was the template, not the parse."," "," ## GM answer conventions learned"," - Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored."]},{"oldStart":143,"oldLines":61,"newStart":153,"newLines":61,"lines":[" - JSON lists -- compact, double quotes, no spaces; ORDER depends on the field:","   - `zip.central_directory_member_names`: full stored paths in CD order (`[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]`).","   - `ooxml.external_relationship_targets`: Target strings SORTED ascending (D15 all modes); rels-file order REJECTED.","-  - `*-synthesis-<algo>-order`: member names ordered by hex digest ascending (D15 TT/Mastery; norm `case_insensitive`).","+  - `*-synthesis-<algo>-order`: member names ordered by hex digest ascending (D15-D19 TT/Mastery; `case_insensitive`).","   Heuristic: a list read off one on-disk structure that the field name calls \"names in the directory\" keeps disk","   order; a set gathered across parts (\"targets\", \"dependencies\") is sorted. If an order is rejected, try the other.","-- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 Machine","-  `0x014c`, u32 AddressOfEntryPoint `0x00065bd0`. Width from the STRUCT, not the id. (Magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`;","-  the binary lane's machine wants `i386` and accepted unpadded entry points -- different generator.)","+- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 PE Machine","+  `0x014c`, u16 ELF e_machine `0x003e` (D19), u32 AddressOfEntryPoint `0x00065bd0`. Width from the STRUCT / the","+  `_uNN_` in the id; the value from the file's own byte order (ELF EI_DATA). (Magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; the","+  binary lane's machine wants `i386` and accepted unpadded entry points -- different generator.)"," - GUIDs: .NET MVID `Guid.ToString()` lowercase no braces (D12); MSI ProductCode the stored string uppercase WITH braces","   (D13). Spelling follows the source, not answer_format."," - Windows paths (`lnk.target_path_windows`): stored LinkInfo path verbatim (backslashes, case, drive letter, no quotes)."," - Version-resource strings (`pe.version_<field>`): StringFileInfo value verbatim incl. extension."," - URLs (`ooxml` Targets): the attribute value verbatim -- scheme, host, path as stored; no trailing-slash or case fixups."," - E-mail headers (`email.<field>`): header value as stored after RFC 5322 unfolding; Message-ID WITH `<>` (D16).","-  Unverified siblings: address fields likely bare `addr-spec` when the field says `_address`, else the full header."," - Media codec names (`media.*codec_name`, D17): FFmpeg/ffprobe `codec_name`, lowercase: WAV tag 1 -> `pcm_u8` (8-bit) /","   `pcm_s16le` / `pcm_s24le` / `pcm_s32le` (RIFX -> `..be`); tag 3 -> `pcm_f32le`/`pcm_f64le`; 6 `pcm_alaw`; 7","   `pcm_mulaw`; 2 `adpcm_ms`; 0x11 `adpcm_ima_wav`; 0x55 `mp3`; 0xFFFE -> SubFormat GUID first u16. Others: `mp3`, `aac`,","-  `opus`, `vorbis`, `flac`, `alac`, `amr_nb`/`amr_wb`, `ac3`. Only `pcm_s16le` is GM-verified. `primary_audio_` = first","-  audio stream in container order (ffprobe `a:0`).","+  `opus`, `vorbis`, `flac`, `alac`, `amr_nb`/`amr_wb`, `ac3`. Only `pcm_s16le` is GM-verified."," - Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` (D10, unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-file-order target list (D15);","   bracket-less Message-ID (D16). Pattern: delimiters that are part of the stored value (`{}`, `<>`) stay."," - Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_` = SOF header, `eocd_total_entries` = the EOCD's own claim,","-  `external_relationship_targets` = rels `Target` where `TargetMode=External`) -- read it literally to pick the","-  structure. A claimed count is NOT a CD walk; CD names are NOT local-header names; `_uNN_hex` fixes read+print width.","+  `e_machine` = Elf_Ehdr member) -- read it literally to pick the structure. A claimed count is NOT a CD walk; CD","+  names are NOT local-header names; `_uNN_hex` fixes read+print width. Unverified ELF siblings: bare enum-ish fields","+  (`ei_data`, `e_type`) have no GM spelling yet -- lib emits `ELFDATA2LSB` / `2`; prefer the `_hex` form if offered."," "," ## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)"," - Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (filename questions: artifact = the zip only).","-- Mastery zip-of-zips (days 1,2,4,5,7,8,10,11,14,15): ONE download (`...-evidence-01.zip`; D15 `evidence-01.zip`)","-  holding `-01.zip`..`-0N.zip`, each holding its set's member(s) (D7 three levels; D8/D15 five full kits, D15 ~606 KB","-  each). Refs `<set zip> -> <member>`; every set reuses member names -> resolve by (set zip, member).","+- Mastery zip-of-zips (days 1,2,4,5,7,8,10,11,14,15-19): ONE download (`...-evidence-01.zip`; D15+ `evidence-01.zip`)","+  holding `-01.zip`..`-0N.zip`, each holding its set's member(s) (D7 three levels; D8/D15+ five full kits). Refs","+  `<set zip> -> <member>`; every set reuses member names -> resolve by (set zip, member)."," - Mastery day 9: download named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip` while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip` ->","   resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not its filename."," - Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` refs."," - Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) -- never hardcode names."," "," ## Pitfalls that cost time","+- **Synthesis dispatch lost AGAIN (D15, D16, D17, D19)**: every day the single's `solve.py` answers the new field but the","+  timed kit adds `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-sha256-order` -> `solver_incomplete` -> an offline generalize (~1 min per","+  mode). D18 was clean only because the single worker pre-wired it. Right after single CORRECT: `grep -n synthesis","+  solver/solve.py` must show a dispatch calling `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order`, with the artifacts root set INSIDE","+  the per-set worker (`_solve_pairs`; Mastery forks one process per set), plus identity for ANY member stem and every","+  carry-over family. Start from the previous day's solver, not a fresh template."," - Id-slug parsing (D16, 1 wrong): ids repeat the fmt word (`d16-email-001-email-message-id`); a regex on the first","   `email-` yields `001-email-message-id` -> lookup miss -> `none`. Anchor `-\\d+-<fmt>-(.+)$`. Never submit `none`","   without grepping the bytes for the field -- `none` means absent in the artifact, not \"my parser returned None\".","-- Registry misses (D14 key one suffix short `lnk.target_path`; D16 fmt `eml` vs GM `email`; D17 `wav.*` vs `media.*`;","-  new families arrive under ABSTRACT fmt words -- D18 reused `media` for video and the prebuilt registry HIT; expect","-  `image`/`archive`/`disk`/`log` next):","+- Registry misses (D14 key one suffix short `lnk.target_path`; D16 fmt `eml` vs GM `email`; D17 `wav.*` vs `media.*`):","   `python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print([k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'])\"` and grep","-  `lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` for the FIELD name; call the nearest extractor directly before writing one.","-- Timed field set != single field set, and the synthesis handler is NOT inherited (D15-D17 lost it ->","-  `solver_incomplete` + offline generalize; D18 the single worker pre-wired it right after CORRECT -> both timed modes","-  first try -- keep doing that): `grep -n synthesis solver/solve.py` must show a dispatch calling","-  `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order`, with the artifacts root set INSIDE the per-set worker (`_solve_pairs`; Mastery","-  forks one process per set), plus identity for ANY member stem and every carry-over family.","+  `lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` for the FIELD name; call the nearest extractor directly before writing one. D18 (`media`)","+  and D19 (`elf`) both HIT the prebuilt registry -> answered in the race probe.","+- Endianness (D19 pun): never `struct.unpack('<H')` an ELF/Mach-O field blindly -- EI_DATA (ELF @5) / the Mach-O magic","+  byte order decide; ELF32 vs ELF64 moves every offset after e_version (e_entry/e_phoff/e_shoff widths)."," - Video geometry has FOUR sources (D18 they agreed; \"crops / impossible device\" flavor says variants won't): stsd","-  sample-entry w/h, codec SPS (h264 frame_cropping -> ffprobe `width`/`height`; MB-aligned size = `coded_width`),","-  tkhd 16.16 display w/h (post-SAR/clap), tkhd matrix rotation (ffprobe keeps coded dims; `rotation` = -90 for","-  portrait phones). `primary_video_dimensions` = ffprobe width x height; prebuilt `media_video.py` reads stsd (+SPS","-  only for pix_fmt/profile) -- if a variant's stsd and SPS disagree, trust the SPS-cropped size and say so in NOTES.","-- Field suffix picks the spelling: `_u16_hex` = the raw struct value (D9: not `i386`/GOARCH); `_codec_name` = the","-  tool vocabulary (D17: `pcm_s16le`, not the raw format tag `1` nor mediainfo's `PCM`).","+  sample-entry w/h, codec SPS (h264 frame_cropping -> ffprobe `width`/`height`), tkhd 16.16 display w/h, tkhd matrix","+  rotation (ffprobe keeps coded dims). If a variant's stsd and SPS disagree, trust the SPS-cropped size, note it.","+- Field suffix picks the spelling: `_u16_hex` = the raw struct value (D9: not `i386`/GOARCH; D19: not `x86-64`);","+  `_codec_name` = the tool vocabulary (D17: `pcm_s16le`, not the raw format tag `1` nor mediainfo's `PCM`)."," - JSON list ORDER (D15, 1 wrong + ~26 s): \"exact values and order\" does not say WHICH order. File order was rejected","   for rels targets; sorted won. Decide per field (conventions above) before the first submit."," - Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (D2 TT); a pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the 409"]},{"oldStart":207,"oldLines":14,"newStart":217,"newLines":14,"lines":["   zip-of-zips returned `PK` as the \"magic\". Resolve the named member's bytes first (recurse), then parse."," - Name-list fields: emit CD bytes as-is for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `\\`, dupes). Decoy names (`*-with-bom.txt`,","   `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF): bytes win every time.","-- Timed windows are seconds; most of it is GM round-trips (D15 start 1.0 s + submit 1.1 s). Parse in memory, never","-  shell out/extract to disk in-window; decompress each member once and cache by (set zip, member) (1.2 MB exe x5).","-- Fresh member family = copy the previous day's solver first (it answers every earlier family), then add only the new","-  handler -- D8 27 s / D9 47 s that way; re-typing older branches cost D12 ~50 s.","+- Timed windows are seconds; most of it is GM round-trips (D19 start 2.4-2.8 s + download 2.7-3.2 s + submit 1.9 s;","+  solve ~1 s). Parse in memory, never shell out/extract to disk in-window; decompress each member once, cache by","+  (set zip, member)."," - Normalizing a stored value (D13): don't strip braces/reshape a stored string because answer_format sounds generic."," - Hex width (D10): `\"0x%x\"` drops leading zeros; print `0x%0{2*size}x`. `_rva` = raw field, never ImageBase + it.","-  Require `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew before any PE field.","+  Require `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew before any PE field; require `\\x7fELF` before any ELF field."," - Harness: `hctf start` on a solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` (D2) -- restore from `log.jsonl`."," - Tools installed: exiftool, poppler, qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck, zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost,","-  mediainfo, sqlite3, ImageMagick, olevba/oleid, olefile, pefile, LnkParse3, dnfile, mutagen (.venv); msitools under","-  tools/msitools; ffmpeg 7.0.2 (no ffprobe) at `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2` (not on PATH). NOT installed: ffprobe, sox.","+  mediainfo, sqlite3, ImageMagick, readelf/objdump, olevba/oleid, olefile, pefile, pyelftools, LnkParse3, dnfile,","+  mutagen (.venv); msitools under tools/msitools; ffmpeg 7.0.2 (no ffprobe) at","+  `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2` (not on PATH). NOT installed: ffprobe, sox."]}],"originalFile":"# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-18; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- Every day = ONE evidence zip (plain Deflate, no password so far). D1-7: one tiny member, ONE structural fact. D8-9:\n  the cumulative kit, every field in every mode. D10-14: one member + one field everywhere. **D15+ split the modes**:\n  single = 1 field (the new member), TT = cumulative kit (D15 20 -> D18 23 fields, +1 per day = the day's new member),\n  Mastery = 5 kits x the TT set, incl. a cross-member \"synthesis\" question every day. Pre-arm EVERY earlier family AND\n  the synthesis before the timed run; the timed field set is not the single's.\n- Member families: note/text -> jpg -> png -> pdf -> inner zip -> Go PE (D9-11) -> .NET dll (D12) -> MSI (D13) -> LNK\n  (D14) -> OOXML `.docx` (D15) -> `.eml` (D16) -> RIFF/WAVE audio (D17) -> MP4 h264+aac video (D18). The fmt word is\n  the GM's ABSTRACT namespace, not the container: `email` (not `eml`), `media` for BOTH audio (D17) and video (D18) --\n  and media fields use ffprobe's vocabulary.\n- A new `<fmt>.<field>` each day: identity -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` -> `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` ->\n  `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries` -> `zip.central_directory_member_names`\n  -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` -> `pe.version_original_filename` ->\n  `dotnet.mvid_guid` -> `msi.product_code_guid` -> `lnk.target_path_windows` -> `ooxml.external_relationship_targets` ->\n  `email.message_id` -> `media.primary_audio_codec_name` -> `media.primary_video_dimensions`. The question names the\n  field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); ids `dNN-<family>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`); `dNN` = the\n  family's first day; `<family>` != `<fmt>` for media (`d17-audio-001-media-`, `d18-video-001-media-`).\n- The flavor text promises extra findings (\"the collision\", \"the impossible destination\", \"equivalent recordings\",\n  \"crops, the recording that could not have come from the claimed device\") that were NEVER asked; the sample usually\n  delivers less (D9 \"several architectures\" -> one i386 PE). The graded field is the STRUCTURAL truth from header bytes;\n  names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. Pre-arm siblings without guessing spellings. Titles are puns.\n- Singles: D1-9 first-submit CORRECT ~27-60 s; D10, D13, D15 lost ONE submit to a convention (padding, braces, list\n  order); D16 lost TWO (parser -> `none`, stripped brackets); D17 ~24 s; D18 ~5 s (race probe answered from the prebuilt\n  `lib.meta` registry before any LLM work). TT/Mastery: first GM submit CORRECT since D4, but D15-D17 only after an\n  offline generalize (synthesis missing); D18 in-window first try (single worker pre-wired the synthesis).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\". Container NAMES drift: D1-14 `metadata-day-NN-evidence[-0N].zip`;\n  D15-18 TT `evidence.zip`, Mastery `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..05.zip`. Route by the ref's text before\n  `->` and by sha256, never a hard-coded name.\n- **Field-set size** -- per mode: D7 TT 11 / Mastery 22; D8-9 12-13 everywhere; D10-14 one; D15 1/20/100; D16 1/21/105;\n  D17 1/22/110; D18 1/23/115. Families: identity + `d04-jpeg-*`, `d05-png-*`, `d06-pdf-*`, `d07-zip-*` (eocd + CD\n  names), `d09-pe-*` (machine, entry RVA, OriginalFilename), `d12-dotnet-*`, `d13-msi-*`, `d14-lnk-*`, `d15-ooxml-*`,\n  `d16-email-*`, `d17-audio-*`, `d18-video-*` + synthesis. Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX (reference solver answering\n  all 23: `challenges/day18/metadata-frame-of-reference/solver/solve.py`).\n- **fmt word vs registry key vs id family word** (D16-D18) -- D16 `email.*` (prebuilt said `eml`); D17\n  `media.primary_audio_codec_name` id `d17-audio-...`; D18 `media.primary_video_dimensions` id `d18-video-...` (one\n  `media` namespace spans two families). Vocabulary = ffprobe (`primary_<type>_` = first stream of that type in\n  container order, `codec_name` = FFmpeg id, `dimensions` = `<width>x<height>`). Rule: take `<fmt>.<field>` from the\n  QUESTION text (or the slug after `-NNN-`), map fmt synonyms (`email`<->`eml`/`mime`; `media`<->`audio`/`video`/`av`/\n  `wav`/`mp4`/...), route the extractor by the member's MAGIC, fall back to the same field under any fmt.\n- **Identity member roster** (D15+) -- THREE small text members (`evidence-note.txt` 33 B, `evidence-note-copy.txt`\n  33 B, `roster.csv` 29 B); EACH identity question picks one at random per set: ids `<member-stem>-{filename,size-bytes,\n  md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}`. The filename question's artifact = the container only\n  (\"the exact filename of the roster\") -> map the id stem to the member. Never assume `evidence-note-*`.\n- **Synthesis / cross-member** (D15+) -- id `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<algo>-order` (TODAY's NN), kind `json`, norm\n  `case_insensitive`: \"Compute the full-file SHA-256 digest of each named file, then submit a compact JSON array of\n  their filenames in ascending digest order. Files: [...]\". The `artifact` names ONE member; the inputs are the\n  `Files:` list, same container. Rule: regex `Files:\\s*(\\[.*?\\])`, resolve each under the ref's container,\n  `hashlib.new(algo)` over raw bytes, sort by hex digest (descending only if said), emit names --\n  `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo)`, get_bytes bound to the artifacts root INSIDE the per-set\n  worker. Shape: note + 2 re-picked kit members (jpg/exe/docx D15, png/dll D17, png/msi D18) + TODAY's member; order\n  re-rolls per set. Only sha256 seen so far -- expect md5/sha1/size/time siblings.\n- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree with the\n  header: answer from the structural bytes of the member the question names.\n- **Member values** -- re-roll per variant; never cache across sets. Seen re-rolled: note case id; D7 entry count\n  2-5; jpg/png dims per set (423x1089, 1255x1059); D10 entry RVA; D11 PE arch (0x014c/0x8664/0xaa64, OriginalFilename\n  `pe-base-<goarch>.exe` follows); D12 MVID; synthesis order. Constant so far (don't rely on it): D13 ProductCode,\n  D14 lnk target, D15 docx targets, kit exe/dll/msi/lnk, D17 codec `pcm_s16le`, D18 video `320x180` (h264 High 10 fps;\n  stsd = tkhd = SPS, identity matrix, pasp 1:1 in every set) -- the flavor's transcodes/crops/rotations are still due.\n- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes case-insensitive; `0x`-hex is `trim` only -> lowercase),\n  `enum` (`accepted_values`), `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact values and order\"). Emit per kind; read\n  `syntax` for prefix/case. JSON ORDER is field-specific -- see conventions.\n- **Question-text tags** -- D9 timed: ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<64 hex>]` suffix; D15+ timed: ``Inspect `<member>`. ``\n  prefix. Strip both before reading names; route by id + `artifact`.\n- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer\n  from an enclosing zip. An OOXML member is itself a zip -- parse it as the asked member, not as a wrapper to descend.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | python `zipfile` read of the member in memory (`7z l -slt` for orientation) |\n| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the member bytes; the id stem names WHICH member |\n| \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |\n| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`) -> `true`/`false` |\n| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width |\n| `png.ihdr_*` | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n| `zip.eocd_*` | of the NAMED zip: last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+10 total entries, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 (`PK\\x06\\x07` -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32) |\n| `zip.central_directory_*` | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from cd offset: name len @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name @+46. Raw stored path, CD order, no dedupe/sort; UTF-8 if flag 0x800 else UTF-8-then-cp437 |\n| `pdf.header_version` | `head -c 16 f | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; catalog `/Version` is a diagnostic only |\n| `pe.coff_*` | `MZ` -> e_lfanew u32 @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` -> Machine u16 @+4; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b`/`0x20b`) |\n| `pe.address_of_entry_point_*` / `pe.image_base*` | opt = e_lfanew+24: AddressOfEntryPoint u32 @opt+16 (RVA); ImageBase @opt+28 (PE32) / u64 @opt+24 (PE32+). objdump \"start address\" is the VA |\n| `pe.version_*` | `pefile` resource dir only -> `FileInfo..StringTable..entries`; id tail -> key ignoring case/`-_`. Shell: `strings -e l f.exe \\| grep -A1 OriginalFilename` |\n| `elf.*` / `macho.*` (promised, not yet asked) | ELF `\\x7fELF`, EI_DATA @5, e_machine u16 @18. Mach-O `feedface`/`feedfacf` cputype @4; fat `cafebabe` BE nfat_arch @4 |\n| `dotnet.*` / Mono assembly | data dir 14 -> CLI header -> `BSJB` -> `#~` (HeapSizes @+6, Valid @+8, rows @+24) -> Module row 0 Mvid (1-based #GUID idx) -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..)`. `lib/meta/dotnet.py` |\n| `msi.*` / `.msi` (OLE `d0 cf 11 e0`) | fast: `strings -n 6 x.msi \\| grep -aoE 'ProductCode\\{[0-9A-F-]{36}\\}'`; exact: CFB streams -> `!_StringPool`/`!_StringData` -> `!Property` (column-major). `olefile` in venv; `day13/.../solve.py msi_property` |\n| `lnk.*` / `.lnk` (`4c 00 00 00` + CLSID 00021401) | LinkFlags @0x14 (0x1 IDList, 0x2 LinkInfo, 0x80 Unicode); target = LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+CommonPathSuffix) verbatim, else IDList. `lib.meta.lnk:target_path` |\n| `ooxml.*` / `.docx/.xlsx/.pptx` (`PK` + `[Content_Types].xml`) | it's a zip of XML parts. Relationships live in EVERY `*.rels` part (`_rels/.rels`, `word/_rels/document.xml.rels`, header/footer/settings rels). External = `TargetMode=\"External\"` (case-insensitive; absent = Internal). `unzip -p f.docx '*.rels' \\| grep -o 'Target=\"[^\"]*\" TargetMode=\"External\"'`; solver: `zipfile` + ElementTree over every `.rels`, local-name `Relationship`. Core props (`docProps/core.xml`) prebuilt in `lib/meta/prebuilt/ooxml.py`; external rels NOT prebuilt as of D15 |\n| `email.*` / `.eml` (text `From:`/`Message-ID:`/`MIME-Version:`, CRLF) | `grep -ai '^message-id' f.eml` to see the stored value; solver: `lib.meta.prebuilt.eml.eml_value(data, {\"field\": f})` (stdlib `email` parser, unfolded raw header). Header values VERBATIM (Message-ID keeps `<...>`). Threading cues (\"replies, forwards, duplicates\") = `In-Reply-To`/`References`/`Message-ID` |\n| `media.*` / audio (`RIFF..WAVE`, `ID3`/`ff fb`, `OggS`, `fLaC`, `ftyp`, `1a 45 df a3`, `FORM..AIFF`, `#!AMR`) | route by MAGIC (names/extensions lie: \"renamed, transcoded\"). WAV: walk RIFF chunks from @12 to `fmt ` -> wFormatTag u16 @+8, bits u16 @+22 (0xFFFE -> SubFormat GUID's first u16 @+32); map to FFmpeg names (Conventions). ground truth = FFmpeg vocabulary: no ffprobe, but `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2 -hide_banner -i f` prints `Stream #0:0: Audio: pcm_s16le ([1][0][0][0] / 0x0001), 16000 Hz, mono, s16` + format tags (worker-side; `mediainfo` says `PCM` = wrong vocabulary). In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `media`/`audio`/`av` (~500 prebuilt fields since D17 night). LIST/INFO `INAM` carried `Huntress audio evidence <12 hex>` (correlation id candidate) |\n| `media.*video*` / MP4-MOV (`....ftyp`), MKV/WebM (`1a 45 df a3`), AVI (`RIFF..AVI `) | box walk `moov` -> `trak` whose `mdia/hdlr` type = `vide` (first one = `primary_video_`) -> `stsd` sample entry: w,h u16 BE @entry+32 (`avc1`/`hvc1`/`vp09`/`av01`); also read tkhd w/h (16.16 @end) + matrix (rotation), `pasp` (SAR), `clap`, avcC SPS crop -- in a variant these may DISAGREE (see Pitfalls). In-window: `lib.meta` fmt `media`/`video`/`av` (`prebuilt/media_video.py`, ~100 video fields). Truth: bundled `ffmpeg -hide_banner -i f` -> `Video: h264 (High) (avc1 / 0x31637661), yuv420p(progressive), 320x180 [SAR 1:1 DAR 16:9], 10 fps` |\n| `*-synthesis-<algo>-order` / \"Files: [...]\" in the question | parse the list from the question text, hash each member of the same container, sort by digest, compact JSON of names |\n| GUID field (`*-guid`) | spelling follows the SOURCE: stored string (MSI) verbatim braces+uppercase; binary (.NET) -> lowercase, no braces |\n| exe-extension decoy (`MZ` without `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit |\n| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)`; decide ORDER per field (conventions) |\n| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids | resolve each set's container separately; see delivery layouts |\n\n## Day by day\n**Days 1-14** (one field each, all timed first try): D1 identity -> D2 `magic-prefix-hex-16` -> D3 BOM -> D4 JPEG SOFn\n`<w>x<h>` -> D5 PNG IHDR -> D6 `pdf.header_version` `x.y` -> D7 `zip.eocd_total_entries` of the INNER zip -> D8 CD names\n(compact JSON, CD order) -> D9-11 one Go PE: `coff_machine_u16_hex` `0x014c`, entry RVA `0x%08x` (unpadded REJECTED),\n`version_original_filename` verbatim -> D12 `dotnet.mvid_guid` (`uuid.UUID(bytes_le)` lowercase, no braces) -> D13\n`msi.product_code_guid` (stored WITH braces; brace-less REJECTED) -> D14 `lnk.target_path_windows` (LinkInfo path).\n\n**Days 15-17** (single = 1 new-family field; TT/Mastery = cumulative kit + synthesis): D15 \"A Word to the Wise\"\n`ooxml.external_relationship_targets` (`.docx` rels `TargetMode=\"External\"` -> Targets SORTED; rels order REJECTED,\n+50 s). D16 \"Return to Sender\" `email.message_id` (`message-001.eml`; VERBATIM with `<>`; lost 2 submits: id regex hit\nthe first `email-` -> `none`, then stripped brackets). D17 \"Hear Me Out\" `media.primary_audio_codec_name` (`audio-001.wav`\nRIFF PCM 16-bit mono 16 kHz + LIST/INFO `INAM` -> ffprobe name `pcm_s16le`, not `PCM`/`0x0001`; ~24 s; flavor\n\"transcoded, renamed, embedded in mail, equivalent recordings\" never asked). All three: `synthesis-sha256-order`\nmissing from the day's template -> `solver_incomplete` -> offline generalize -> CORRECT (D17 Mastery also needed the\nartifacts root set inside the per-set worker).\n\n**Day 18 — Frame of Reference** (`media.primary_video_dimensions`, kind `exact_text` \"... use the literal none only when\nthe requested field is absent\", norm `trim`, id `d18-video-001-media-primary-video-dimensions`). Prompt: \"Clips,\npreviews, and screen recordings have been mixed together. Use stream geometry to identify originals, crops, and the\nrecording that could not have come from the claimed device.\" (originals/crops/impossible-device flavor -- NOT asked;\none MP4 only).\n- Artifact: 18.7 KB zip -> `video-001.mp4` (19 775 B, `ftyp isom` minor 512, brands `isomiso2avc1mp41`, Lavf layout\n  `moov` before `mdat`): trak 1 `vide` h264 High `avc1` 320x180 (`avcC`+`pasp` 1:1+`btrt`, 10 fps, 5 frames, encoder\n  `Lavc libx264`), trak 2 `soun` aac LC 44.1 kHz stereo; `udta/meta` mdta `title` = `Huntress MP4 evidence <12 HEX>`.\n  stsd w/h = tkhd 320.0/180.0 = SPS; tkhd matrix identity (rotation 0).\n- Key insight: it's ffprobe `width`x`height` of stream v:0 spelled like D4/D5 (`<w>x<h>`, lowercase `x`). The audio\n  trak in the same file must not be picked; the first `vide` handler wins.\n- Tools: none needed by hand -- the race probe answered from the prebuilt `lib.meta` `media_video.py` (D17-night\n  `media-video-streams` gap). Manual check: box walk to `stsd` (entry+32) or the bundled ffmpeg `-i` line above.\n- Single CORRECT on the first submit ~5 s after start (submit RTT 1.2 s). The single worker then PRE-WIRED the\n  `synthesis-<algo>-order` dispatch (+ artifacts-root global set in `_solve_pairs`) before the timed runs -> TT 23\n  (in-window 3.5 s) and Mastery 5x23 = 115 (in-window 6.8 s) CORRECT first try, no generalize -- first clean timed day\n  since D14.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`). Booleans: enum `true` / `false`.\n- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR, video `media.primary_video_dimensions` D18): `<width>x<height>`, lowercase\n  `x`, no spaces. Video = ffprobe width/height of v:0 (coded size, NOT rotated, not the tkhd display size).\n- PDF header version: bare `x.y`; absent -> literal `none` (wording; `none` not yet GM-confirmed). Counts: plain integer.\n- JSON lists -- compact, double quotes, no spaces; ORDER depends on the field:\n  - `zip.central_directory_member_names`: full stored paths in CD order (`[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]`).\n  - `ooxml.external_relationship_targets`: Target strings SORTED ascending (D15 all modes); rels-file order REJECTED.\n  - `*-synthesis-<algo>-order`: member names ordered by hex digest ascending (D15 TT/Mastery; norm `case_insensitive`).\n  Heuristic: a list read off one on-disk structure that the field name calls \"names in the directory\" keeps disk\n  order; a set gathered across parts (\"targets\", \"dependencies\") is sorted. If an order is rejected, try the other.\n- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 Machine\n  `0x014c`, u32 AddressOfEntryPoint `0x00065bd0`. Width from the STRUCT, not the id. (Magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`;\n  the binary lane's machine wants `i386` and accepted unpadded entry points -- different generator.)\n- GUIDs: .NET MVID `Guid.ToString()` lowercase no braces (D12); MSI ProductCode the stored string uppercase WITH braces\n  (D13). Spelling follows the source, not answer_format.\n- Windows paths (`lnk.target_path_windows`): stored LinkInfo path verbatim (backslashes, case, drive letter, no quotes).\n- Version-resource strings (`pe.version_<field>`): StringFileInfo value verbatim incl. extension.\n- URLs (`ooxml` Targets): the attribute value verbatim -- scheme, host, path as stored; no trailing-slash or case fixups.\n- E-mail headers (`email.<field>`): header value as stored after RFC 5322 unfolding; Message-ID WITH `<>` (D16).\n  Unverified siblings: address fields likely bare `addr-spec` when the field says `_address`, else the full header.\n- Media codec names (`media.*codec_name`, D17): FFmpeg/ffprobe `codec_name`, lowercase: WAV tag 1 -> `pcm_u8` (8-bit) /\n  `pcm_s16le` / `pcm_s24le` / `pcm_s32le` (RIFX -> `..be`); tag 3 -> `pcm_f32le`/`pcm_f64le`; 6 `pcm_alaw`; 7\n  `pcm_mulaw`; 2 `adpcm_ms`; 0x11 `adpcm_ima_wav`; 0x55 `mp3`; 0xFFFE -> SubFormat GUID first u16. Others: `mp3`, `aac`,\n  `opus`, `vorbis`, `flac`, `alac`, `amr_nb`/`amr_wb`, `ac3`. Only `pcm_s16le` is GM-verified. `primary_audio_` = first\n  audio stream in container order (ffprobe `a:0`).\n- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` (D10, unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-file-order target list (D15);\n  bracket-less Message-ID (D16). Pattern: delimiters that are part of the stored value (`{}`, `<>`) stay.\n- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_` = SOF header, `eocd_total_entries` = the EOCD's own claim,\n  `external_relationship_targets` = rels `Target` where `TargetMode=External`) -- read it literally to pick the\n  structure. A claimed count is NOT a CD walk; CD names are NOT local-header names; `_uNN_hex` fixes read+print width.\n\n## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (filename questions: artifact = the zip only).\n- Mastery zip-of-zips (days 1,2,4,5,7,8,10,11,14,15): ONE download (`...-evidence-01.zip`; D15 `evidence-01.zip`)\n  holding `-01.zip`..`-0N.zip`, each holding its set's member(s) (D7 three levels; D8/D15 five full kits, D15 ~606 KB\n  each). Refs `<set zip> -> <member>`; every set reuses member names -> resolve by (set zip, member).\n- Mastery day 9: download named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip` while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip` ->\n  resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not its filename.\n- Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` refs.\n- Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) -- never hardcode names.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- Id-slug parsing (D16, 1 wrong): ids repeat the fmt word (`d16-email-001-email-message-id`); a regex on the first\n  `email-` yields `001-email-message-id` -> lookup miss -> `none`. Anchor `-\\d+-<fmt>-(.+)$`. Never submit `none`\n  without grepping the bytes for the field -- `none` means absent in the artifact, not \"my parser returned None\".\n- Registry misses (D14 key one suffix short `lnk.target_path`; D16 fmt `eml` vs GM `email`; D17 `wav.*` vs `media.*`;\n  new families arrive under ABSTRACT fmt words -- D18 reused `media` for video and the prebuilt registry HIT; expect\n  `image`/`archive`/`disk`/`log` next):\n  `python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print([k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'])\"` and grep\n  `lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` for the FIELD name; call the nearest extractor directly before writing one.\n- Timed field set != single field set, and the synthesis handler is NOT inherited (D15-D17 lost it ->\n  `solver_incomplete` + offline generalize; D18 the single worker pre-wired it right after CORRECT -> both timed modes\n  first try -- keep doing that): `grep -n synthesis solver/solve.py` must show a dispatch calling\n  `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order`, with the artifacts root set INSIDE the per-set worker (`_solve_pairs`; Mastery\n  forks one process per set), plus identity for ANY member stem and every carry-over family.\n- Video geometry has FOUR sources (D18 they agreed; \"crops / impossible device\" flavor says variants won't): stsd\n  sample-entry w/h, codec SPS (h264 frame_cropping -> ffprobe `width`/`height`; MB-aligned size = `coded_width`),\n  tkhd 16.16 display w/h (post-SAR/clap), tkhd matrix rotation (ffprobe keeps coded dims; `rotation` = -90 for\n  portrait phones). `primary_video_dimensions` = ffprobe width x height; prebuilt `media_video.py` reads stsd (+SPS\n  only for pix_fmt/profile) -- if a variant's stsd and SPS disagree, trust the SPS-cropped size and say so in NOTES.\n- Field suffix picks the spelling: `_u16_hex` = the raw struct value (D9: not `i386`/GOARCH); `_codec_name` = the\n  tool vocabulary (D17: `pcm_s16le`, not the raw format tag `1` nor mediainfo's `PCM`).\n- JSON list ORDER (D15, 1 wrong + ~26 s): \"exact values and order\" does not say WHICH order. File order was rejected\n  for rels targets; sorted won. Decide per field (conventions above) before the first submit.\n- Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (D2 TT); a pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the 409\n  `start_required` body (questions, NO `answer_ids`). Answer under the live `answer_ids`.\n- Don't let the flavor text widen the question: only the named field is graded; extra checks are diagnostics.\n- Container-of-containers: a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded zip reads the OUTER EOCD, a name lookup on\n  zip-of-zips returned `PK` as the \"magic\". Resolve the named member's bytes first (recurse), then parse.\n- Name-list fields: emit CD bytes as-is for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `\\`, dupes). Decoy names (`*-with-bom.txt`,\n  `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF): bytes win every time.\n- Timed windows are seconds; most of it is GM round-trips (D15 start 1.0 s + submit 1.1 s). Parse in memory, never\n  shell out/extract to disk in-window; decompress each member once and cache by (set zip, member) (1.2 MB exe x5).\n- Fresh member family = copy the previous day's solver first (it answers every earlier family), then add only the new\n  handler -- D8 27 s / D9 47 s that way; re-typing older branches cost D12 ~50 s.\n- Normalizing a stored value (D13): don't strip braces/reshape a stored string because answer_format sounds generic.\n- Hex width (D10): `\"0x%x\"` drops leading zeros; print `0x%0{2*size}x`. `_rva` = raw field, never ImageBase + it.\n  Require `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew before any PE field.\n- Harness: `hctf start` on a solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` (D2) -- restore from `log.jsonl`.\n- Tools installed: exiftool, poppler, qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck, zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost,\n  mediainfo, sqlite3, ImageMagick, olevba/oleid, olefile, pefile, LnkParse3, dnfile, mutagen (.venv); msitools under\n  tools/msitools; ffmpeg 7.0.2 (no ffprobe) at `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2` (not on PATH). NOT installed: ffprobe, sox.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UnFm7PMw9YVG9ECVwpFSJQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
