culative built-ins), class/data/type/shnum/phnum/flags, PT_INTERP, build-id, section names | prebuilt elf | `7f 45 4c 46`; EI_CLASS @4, EI_DATA @5, e_machine @18 | `elftools.elf.elffile.ELFFile(io.BytesIO(b))` (I); `readelf -hn` (I) | med (D9 flavor promised archs) |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| 82 | ELF header: e_machine, e_entry, class/data/osabi/type/version/shnum/phnum/flags, PT_INTERP, build-id, section names | seen D19 `elf.e_machine_u16_hex` (`0x003e`, read in EI_DATA order, 4-digit padded); rest prebuilt elf (speculative; `ei_data` -> `ELFDATA2LSB`, `e_type` -> `2` spellings unverified) | `7f 45 4c 46`; EI_CLASS @4, EI_DATA @5, e_type @16, e_machine @18 | `lib.meta` fmt `elf`; `elftools.elf.elffile.ELFFile(io.BytesIO(b))` (I); `readelf -hn` (I) | high -- D20-D22 deeper ELF fields + every timed kit |\"\"\")\nnewrows = \"\"\"\n| 113 | ELF dynamic + notes: DT_NEEDED list, DT_SONAME, DT_RUNPATH/RPATH, `.comment` (GCC/clang/rustc version), NT_GNU_ABI_TAG OS + min kernel (`3.2.0`), `.note.gnu.property` (x86 ISA/IBT/SHSTK), stripped?, dynsym names/count | gap (elf-dynamic-notes) | PT_DYNAMIC / `.dynamic`; `.note.ABI-tag`; `.comment` | pyelftools `iter_tags('DT_NEEDED')` (I); `readelf -dn --string-dump=.comment` (I) | high -- next ELF depth |\n| 114 | ELF ident/header siblings in hex grammar: ei_class/ei_data/ei_osabi `_u8_hex`, e_type/e_version/e_entry/e_phoff/e_shoff/e_flags `_uNN_hex` (width by class), machine/arch NAME vocabularies (readelf, `uname -m`, Go GOARCH, Debian arch) | partial (elf.py; hex `_u8_` forms + name maps = gap elf-ident-hex-siblings) | same header; ELF32 offsets differ after @24 | struct with `'<>'[ei_data-1]`; `readelf -h` (I) | high -- D19 grammar |\n| 115 | Architecture / deployment-group synthesis: group or order ELF+PE+Mach-O members by machine, bitness, endianness, OS ABI, interpreter; the member whose name/extension lies; per-arch counts | gap (elf-arch-synthesis) | synthesis text \"deployment groups\", \"architecture\", \"same platform\"; `Files: [...]` of binaries | lib.meta.synthesis + per-format machine extractors | high -- D19 flavor |\n| 116 | ELF hardening (checksec): PIE, NX (PT_GNU_STACK), RELRO none/partial/full, canary (`__stack_chk_fail`), FORTIFY, RPATH | gap (elf-hardening-checksec) | PT_GNU_STACK / PT_GNU_RELRO / DF_1_PIE / BIND_NOW | pyelftools segments + dynamic (I); `checksec` (M) | med |\n| 117 | Go / Rust build provenance in ELF/PE/Mach-O: `\\\\xff Go buildinf:` go version, module path, GOOS/GOARCH/-ldflags/vcs.revision; `.note.go.buildid`; rustc commit in `.comment`/panic paths | gap (go-rust-buildinfo) | `\\\\xff Go buildinf:`; `Go build ID:`; `/rustc/<40 hex>/` | struct + varint strings; `go version -m` (M) | med-high -- D9-11 Go PE, \"several systems\" = cross-builds |\n| 118 | Bytecode / VM headers: Java class (`cafebabe` major @6 -- collides with Mach-O fat), `.pyc` magic -> Python version, WASM `\\\\0asm` sections/exports, DEX version/checksum/signature | gap (bytecode-headers) | `ca fe ba be` + major >= 45; pyc `XX XX 0d 0a`; `00 61 73 6d`; `dex\\\\n03x\\\\0` | struct; `javap -v` (M); `file -k` (I) | med |\n| 119 | Mach-O deeper: LC_LOAD_DYLIB list, LC_RPATH, LC_MAIN entryoff, segment names, code signature CodeDirectory identifier/teamID/cdhash, entitlements | gap (macho-codesign-dylibs; header fields prebuilt macho) | `fa de 0c c0` SuperBlob, `fa de 0c 02` CodeDirectory, `fa de 71 71` entitlements | struct (BE blobs); `lief.MachO` (I, worker-only); `rabin2 -I` (I) | med-high -- after ELF |\n| 120 | Linux packages: `.deb` (ar `!<arch>`, control Package/Version/Architecture), `.rpm` (lead `ed ab ee db`, header NAME/VERSION/ARCH), AppImage (`AI\\\\x02` @8), squashfs `hsqs` superblock | gap (linux-packages) | `!<arch>\\\\n` / `ed ab ee db` / `hsqs` | struct + tarfile + lzma; `dpkg-deb -I`, `rpm -qip` (M) | med -- \"deployment groups\" |\n| 121 | ELF special objects: ET_REL kernel module `.modinfo` (vermagic, srcversion, license, depends), ET_CORE notes (NT_PRPSINFO fname/psargs, NT_FILE), U-Boot uImage `27 05 19 56` firmware headers | gap (elf-core-ko-firmware) | e_type 1/4; `.modinfo`; uImage magic | pyelftools notes (I); `modinfo` (M) | low-med |\n\"\"\"\nlines=s.split('\\n')\ni=[k for k,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 112 |')][0]\nlines.insert(i+1,newrows.strip('\\n'))\ns='\\n'.join(lines)\nrep(\"\"\"7f 45 4c 46                       ELF     elftools ELFFile(io.BytesIO(b)); readelf -hn\ncf fa ed fe / ce fa ed fe / ca fe ba be  Mach-O / fat   struct; rabin2 -I; lief\"\"\",\n\"\"\"7f 45 4c 46                       ELF     EI_CLASS@4 (1=32,2=64) EI_DATA@5 (1=LE,2=BE) -> unpack EVERYTHING in that order:\n  e_type u16@16, e_machine u16@18 (D19 `0x003e` = 4-digit padded), e_entry@24; lib.meta fmt `elf`; readelf -hdn\n  machines: 0x0003 i386 0x0008 mips 0x0014 ppc 0x0015 ppc64 0x0016 s390 0x0028 arm 0x003e x86-64 0x00b7 aarch64 0x00f3 riscv\ncf fa ed fe / ce fa ed fe / ca fe ba be  Mach-O / fat (cafebabe + major@6 >= 45 = Java class)   struct; rabin2 -I; lief\"\"\")\n# JSON block\nm=re.search(r\"```json\\n(.*?)\\n```\",s,re.S)\ngaps=json.loads(m.group(1))\ngaps=[g for g in gaps if g['id']!='elf-header']\nbyid={g['id']:g for g in gaps}\nfor gid in ['media-image-as-video-stream','video-geometry-crop-aspect','video-device-provenance','mp4-mov-atoms','video-geometry-synthesis','image-modern-containers','media-codec-params']:\n    byid[gid]['priority']=2\nbyid['macho-header']['priority']=1\nbyid['macho-header']['detail']=\"Built (fmt macho: cputype/filetype/flags `_u32_hex`, ncmds, LC_UUID, fat nfat_arch/cputypes, build version). D19 ELF + flavor 'several systems' -> Mach-O is the likeliest next binary family; verify cputype spelling `0x01000007` (u32, 8 digits) for x86_64 / `0x0100000c` arm64 and that fat slices are read BE while thin headers follow the magic's byte order. Deeper load commands = macho-codesign-dylibs.\"\nbyid['synthesis-siblings']['detail']+=\" D19: Files = note + document-001.pdf + shortcut-001.lnk + collector-001.elf; the single worker added an ELF extractor but NOT the synthesis branch -> TT and Mastery solver_incomplete -> offline generalize ported D18's branch. 4 of 5 timed days lost this way: the day's solver must start from the previous day's solve.py.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"elf-dynamic-notes\",\"concept\":\"ELF dynamic section + notes (DT_NEEDED, SONAME, RUNPATH, .comment, ABI tag, gnu.property)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt elf (alias binary/linux). Fields: dt_needed / needed_libraries (compact JSON list in DT order), dt_soname / soname, dt_runpath / runpath, dt_rpath / rpath (verbatim or none), comment / comment_strings (.comment NUL-split, verbatim e.g. `GCC: (Ubuntu 11.4.0-1ubuntu1~22.04) 11.4.0`), abi_tag_os (NT_GNU_ABI_TAG desc u32[0]: 0 Linux, 1 GNU/Hurd, 2 Solaris, 3 FreeBSD) + abi_tag_kernel / min_kernel_version (`3.2.0`), gnu_property_x86_isa_needed / x86_feature_1 (IBT/SHSTK), is_stripped (no .symtab -> true), dynsym_count, symtab_count, dynamic_symbol_names (imports, sorted + DT order variants), init_array_count, e_phentsize, e_ehsize, pt_load_count, program_header_types (JSON list in phdr order: PT_PHDR,PT_INTERP,...). Honour EI_CLASS/EI_DATA for every struct (synthesize a 32-bit MSB fixture too). pyelftools is allowlisted; pure struct is fine. Fixture: day19 collector-001.elf (x86-64 ET_EXEC, interp ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, ABI tag GNU/Linux 3.2.0, stripped, no build-id).\"},\n {\"id\":\"elf-ident-hex-siblings\",\"concept\":\"ELF ident/header fields in the GM `_uNN_hex` grammar + architecture name vocabularies\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D19 field `elf.e_machine_u16_hex` = raw Elf_Ehdr member, `0x` + zero-padded to struct width, read in EI_DATA order. lib/meta/prebuilt/elf.py already has e_machine_u16_hex, e_type_u16_hex, e_flags_u32_hex, e_entry_hex, ei_class/ei_data/ei_osabi (as names `ELFDATA2LSB`/`ELFOSABI_NONE`), e_type (`2`). Add the hex/width grammar for every header member: ei_class_u8_hex (`0x02`), ei_data_u8_hex (`0x01`), ei_osabi_u8_hex, ei_abiversion_u8_hex, ei_version_u8_hex, e_version_u32_hex (`0x00000001`), e_entry_u64_hex / e_entry_u32_hex (16 vs 8 digits by class; `e_entry_hex` width = class), e_phoff_*_hex, e_shoff_*_hex, e_ehsize/e_phentsize/e_phnum/e_shentsize/e_shnum/e_shstrndx (integers + `_u16_hex`), e_type_name (`ET_EXEC`/`ET_DYN`), plus vocabularies: machine_name (readelf `Advanced Micro Devices X86-64`), architecture / arch (`x86_64`, `aarch64`, `i386`, `arm`, `mips`, `ppc64le` uname-style), goarch (`amd64`/`arm64`/`386`), endianness (`little`/`big`), bitness / elf_class (`64`/`ELF64`). Fixtures: day19 elf + synthesized ELF32 MSB MIPS (e_machine 0x0008) + ELF32 LSB ARM (0x0028, e_flags 0x05000400) + ELF64 MSB s390x (0x0016).\"},\n {\"id\":\"elf-arch-synthesis\",\"concept\":\"Cross-file architecture / deployment-group synthesis over ELF + PE + Mach-O members\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D19 flavor 'Linux binaries from several systems have been pooled with Windows executables and renamed data ... rebuild deployment groups' (never asked yet; the D19 synthesis was still sha256-order). Add lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis_arch.py over the `Files: [...]` list (same contract as lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order): classify each member by MAGIC (ELF/PE/Mach-O/fat/other) -> canonical (format, machine u16/u32 hex, bitness, endianness, os). Fields (fmt synthesis, id tail): architecture_groups / deployment_groups (compact JSON list of lists, members in Files order, groups ordered by first appearance; plus object {arch:[names]} variant keyed by uname-style arch), elf_members / non_elf_members (names whose magic is ELF, Files order), odd_architecture_member, machine_order (names sorted by machine value then name), count_<arch>. Treat a renamed non-binary as format `data`. Fixture: day19 TT kit (collector-001.elf, telemetry-agent-001.exe, managed-001.dll + a synthesized BE ELF).\"},\n {\"id\":\"elf-hardening-checksec\",\"concept\":\"ELF hardening flags (PIE, NX, RELRO, canary, FORTIFY)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt elf: pie (ET_DYN with PT_INTERP or DF_1_PIE -> true), nx (PT_GNU_STACK present and !PF_X), relro (`none`/`partial`/`full`: PT_GNU_RELRO + DT_BIND_NOW or DF_1_NOW), canary (`__stack_chk_fail` in dynsym), fortify (`__*_chk` imports), executable_stack, textrel. Booleans `true`/`false`. Fixture: day19 elf (ET_EXEC -> pie false).\"},\n {\"id\":\"go-rust-buildinfo\",\"concept\":\"Go buildinfo / build ID and Rust toolchain provenance inside ELF/PE/Mach-O\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt go (aliases golang, elf, pe, macho): find `\\\\xff Go buildinf:` (16-B header; ptr size @14, flags @15; flags&2 -> inline varint-prefixed strings: Go version `go1.22.3`, then modinfo text with `path`, `mod`, `dep`, `build\\\\tGOOS=linux`, `build\\\\tGOARCH=arm64`, `-ldflags`, `vcs.revision`, `vcs.time`); fields go_version, module_path, main_module_version, goos, goarch, build_settings (JSON object), vcs_revision, go_build_id (`\\\\xff Go build ID: \\\"...\\\"` / ELF note `.note.go.buildid` type 4 'Go'). Rust: rustc_version from `.comment` `rustc version 1.xx.y (hash date)`, rustc_commit from `/rustc/<40 hex>/library` paths. Fixtures: day09-11 Go PE (pe-base-<goarch>.exe).\"},\n {\"id\":\"bytecode-headers\",\"concept\":\"Java class / .pyc / WASM / DEX headers (and the cafebabe Mach-O-fat collision)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt java (alias class/jvm): magic_u32_hex `0xcafebabe`, minor_version, major_version (52=Java 8, 55=11, 61=17, 65=21), java_version, constant_pool_count, this_class name, access_flags_u16_hex. Disambiguate from Mach-O fat (u32 BE @4: fat nfat_arch small; class minor<<16|major with major>=45). fmt pyc: magic_u16 (LE) -> python_version table (3.8 3413, 3.9 3425, 3.10 3439, 3.11 3495, 3.12 3531, 3.13 3571), flags_u32_hex, source_mtime_utc, source_size. fmt wasm: version_u32, section_ids/custom_section_names/export_names (JSON). fmt dex: version (`035`/`039`), checksum_u32_hex (adler32), signature_sha1_hex, file_size, string_ids_size, class_defs_size.\"},\n {\"id\":\"macho-codesign-dylibs\",\"concept\":\"Mach-O load-command depth: dylibs, rpaths, entry, segments, code signature, entitlements\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt macho: load_dylib_names (LC_LOAD_DYLIB/LC_LOAD_WEAK_DYLIB/LC_REEXPORT_DYLIB paths, command order JSON), rpaths, id_dylib, main_entryoff_u64_hex (LC_MAIN), segment_names, section_names (`__TEXT,__text`), source_version, code signature: LC_CODE_SIGNATURE dataoff -> SuperBlob `fa de 0c c0` (BE) -> CodeDirectory `fa de 0c 02` identifier, team_id, hash_type, cdhash (hash of the CD blob, first 20 B hex), entitlements (`fa de 71 71` XML plist keys JSON), is_adhoc_signed. Per-slice for fat (slice index or cputype selector). Fixtures: synthesize minimal thin x86_64 + arm64 + fat headers with struct (no macOS toolchain here).\"},\n {\"id\":\"linux-packages\",\"concept\":\"Linux deployment packages: .deb / .rpm / AppImage / squashfs headers\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D19 'rebuild deployment groups'. fmt deb: ar `!<arch>\\\\n` members (60-B headers) debian-binary (`2.0`), control.tar.{gz,xz,zst} -> ./control Package/Version/Architecture/Maintainer/Depends, member_names (ar order); fmt rpm: lead `ed ab ee db` (name 66 B @10, arch u16 @6?), header `8e ad e8 01` index entries -> NAME 1000, VERSION 1001, RELEASE 1002, ARCH 1022, OS 1021, PAYLOADCOMPRESSOR 1125; fmt appimage: ELF with `AI\\\\x02` @8, squashfs offset = end of ELF sections; fmt squashfs: `hsqs` superblock inode count, mkfs_time_utc, block_size, compression id (1 gzip 2 lzma 3 lzo 4 xz 5 lz4 6 zstd), version. zstd not in stdlib -> `none` for zstd-only fields.\"},\n {\"id\":\"elf-core-ko-firmware\",\"concept\":\"ELF relocatables / kernel modules / core dumps and firmware image headers\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt elf: modinfo_<key> from `.modinfo` NUL-separated `key=value` (vermagic, srcversion, license, name, depends, author); core dumps (e_type 4): NT_PRPSINFO pr_fname/pr_psargs, NT_FILE mapped paths JSON, NT_PRSTATUS count (threads), NT_AUXV AT_EXECFN. fmt uimage: U-Boot legacy `27 05 19 56` BE header: hcrc/dcrc_u32_hex, time_utc, size, load/entry_u32_hex, os/arch/type/comp names, image_name (32 B NUL-trimmed).\"},\n]\nids_existing={g['id'] for g in gaps}\nfor g in new: assert g['id'] not in ids_existing\ngaps=gaps+new\ngaps.sort(key=lambda g:g['priority'])  # stable\nout=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\"\ns=s[:m.start(1)]+out+s[m.end(1):]\ns=s.replace(\"Ranking (D18 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D19-D21 question\",\"Ranking (D19 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D20-D22 question\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n 'Ranking (D19' reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md | cut -c1-80"}}}
